4
00:01:01.136 --> 00:01:04.466
POLAND. 1944

5
00:02:18.769 --> 00:02:22.490
Westchester. New York 1944

6
00:02:48.950 --> 00:02:51.541
Mother. what are you...

7
00:02:52.218 --> 00:02:54.039
I thought you were a burglar.

8
00:02:54.657 --> 00:02:57.755
I didn't mean to scare you darling.
I was just getting a snack.

9
00:02:57.849 --> 00:02:59.195
Go back to bed.

10
00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:01.981
What's the matter?

11
00:03:02.717 --> 00:03:04.307
Go on. back to bed.

12
00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:08.816
I'll make you a hot chocolate.

13
00:03:09.423 --> 00:03:10.930
Who are you?

14
00:03:15.212 --> 00:03:17.212
And what have you done with my mother?

15
00:03:17.323 --> 00:03:21.260
<i>**My  mother has never set foot
in this kitchen in her life.**</i>

16
00:03:22.247 --> 00:03:25.139
<i>**And she certainly wouldn't have made me
hot chocolate.**</i>

17
00:03:25.656 --> 00:03:28.693
<i>**Unless she kept ordering me to do it.**</i>

18
00:03:46.607 --> 00:03:49.145
You're not scared of me?

19
00:03:49.146 --> 00:03:52.488
I always believed I couldn't be the
only one in the world.

20
00:03:52.727 --> 00:03:55.177
The only person who is...

21
00:03:55.178 --> 00:03:57.011
...different.

22
00:03:58.428 --> 00:04:02.189
And here you are.
Charles Xavier.

23
00:04:05.191 --> 00:04:06.380
Raven.

24
00:04:07.869 --> 00:04:09.896
You're hungry. and alone?

25
00:04:09.897 --> 00:04:11.499
Take whatever you want.

26
00:04:11.500 --> 00:04:14.040
We've got lots of food.
you don't have to steal.

27
00:04:15.114 --> 00:04:16.360
In fact...

28
00:04:17.842 --> 00:04:20.517
...you never have to steal again.

29
00:04:33.263 --> 00:04:35.847
Understand this. Eric.

30
00:04:36.571 --> 00:04:39.563
These Nazi's I'm not like them.

31
00:04:44.007 --> 00:04:46.840
Genes are the key. yes?

32
00:04:47.283 --> 00:04:49.174
But their goals?

33
00:04:49.407 --> 00:04:54.369
Blue eyes. Blonde hair. pathetic.

34
00:04:56.029 --> 00:04:57.071
Mmm.

35
00:04:59.485 --> 00:05:01.095
Eat the chocolate.

36
00:05:02.416 --> 00:05:03.667
It's good.

37
00:05:04.168 --> 00:05:05.363
Want some?

38
00:05:07.452 --> 00:05:09.333
I want to see my mama.

39
00:05:15.843 --> 00:05:22.081
Genes are the keys that unlocks
the door to a new age. Erik.

40
00:05:22.510 --> 00:05:25.885
A new future for mankind.

41
00:05:26.222 --> 00:05:27.897
Evolution.

42
00:05:28.933 --> 00:05:31.412
You know what I'm talking about?

43
00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:36.262
It's a simple thing I ask of you.

44
00:05:36.399 --> 00:05:41.877
A little coin is nothing compared to a big gate.

45
00:05:42.776 --> 00:05:43.818
Is it.

46
00:05:54.212 --> 00:05:55.255
Yes.

47
00:05:58.890 --> 00:06:01.165
I've tried. Herr Doctor.

48
00:06:01.166 --> 00:06:04.604
I can't...I don't...

49
00:06:05.726 --> 00:06:07.279
It's impossible.

50
00:06:09.578 --> 00:06:15.192
The only thing I can say for the Nazi's.
is their methods seem to produce results.

51
00:06:17.808 --> 00:06:19.775
I'm sorry. Erik.

52
00:06:30.573 --> 00:06:31.615
Mama.

53
00:06:32.665 --> 00:06:34.128
My darling.

54
00:06:34.583 --> 00:06:36.520
How are you?

55
00:06:40.294 --> 00:06:42.212
Here's what we're going to do.

56
00:06:42.958 --> 00:06:45.225
I'm going to count to three.

57
00:06:46.137 --> 00:06:49.275
And you're going to move the coin.

58
00:06:49.762 --> 00:06:54.460
You don't move the coin.
I pull the trigger.

59
00:06:56.271 --> 00:06:58.163
Understand?

60
00:06:59.492 --> 00:07:00.535
One.

61
00:07:01.730 --> 00:07:02.773
Mama.

62
00:07:02.774 --> 00:07:04.251
You can do it.

63
00:07:09.395 --> 00:07:10.438
Two.

64
00:07:13.055 --> 00:07:15.052
Everything is good.

65
00:07:25.477 --> 00:07:27.001
Everything is good.

66
00:07:28.980 --> 00:07:30.579
Everything is good.

67
00:07:31.194 --> 00:07:32.237
Three.

68
00:07:53.473 --> 00:07:55.573
Yes. wonderful!

69
00:08:05.539 --> 00:08:06.582
Excellent.

70
00:08:34.809 --> 00:08:35.852
Noooo.

71
00:08:51.076 --> 00:08:52.912
Outstanding. Erik.

72
00:08:54.105 --> 00:08:57.882
So we unlocked your gift with anger.

73
00:08:58.791 --> 00:09:02.598
Anger and pain.

74
00:09:04.624 --> 00:09:06.129
You and me.

75
00:09:07.405 --> 00:09:10.252
We're going to have a lot of fun together.

76
00:09:57.562 --> 00:10:00.912
Geneva. Switzerland - 1962

77
00:10:13.443 --> 00:10:16.775
Oxford University. England

78
00:10:23.450 --> 00:10:25.517
Hetro-chromia.

79
00:10:27.528 --> 00:10:30.179
A gentlemen would at least offer
to buy me a drink first.

80
00:10:30.180 --> 00:10:34.142
Newman. a pint of bitter for me
and a brandy for the lady. please.

81
00:10:34.616 --> 00:10:36.556
- How did you know that?
- Lucky guess.

82
00:10:36.557 --> 00:10:38.414
The name's. Xavier.
Charles Xavier.

83
00:10:38.415 --> 00:10:39.651
- How do you do...
- Amy.

84
00:10:39.755 --> 00:10:41.725
Hetrochromia. is in reference to your eyes.

85
00:10:41.822 --> 00:10:44.183
which I have to say are stunning.

86
00:10:44.290 --> 00:10:46.668
One green. one blue. It's a mutation.

87
00:10:46.669 --> 00:10:48.174
It's a very groovy mutation.

88
00:10:48.289 --> 00:10:51.647
I've got news for you. Amy.
You are a mutant.

89
00:10:51.648 --> 00:10:54.979
First you proposition a girl.
and then you call her. deformed.

90
00:10:55.212 --> 00:10:57.391
How is that seduction tactic working for you?

91
00:10:57.481 --> 00:10:59.014
I'll tell you in the morning.

92
00:10:59.272 --> 00:11:01.804
No. seriously though. you mustn’t knock it.

93
00:11:01.805 --> 00:11:03.679
Mutation's go from single cell organisms

94
00:11:03.807 --> 00:11:07.118
to being the dominate form of
reproductive life. on this planet.

95
00:11:07.228 --> 00:11:10.357
Infinite forms of variations with each generation.

96
00:11:10.498 --> 00:11:13.626
All through. mutation.

97
00:11:14.753 --> 00:11:16.784
Then let's reclaim that word.

98
00:11:20.647 --> 00:11:22.991
- Mutant. and proud.
- Chin. chin. hey.

99
00:11:23.150 --> 00:11:24.678
Hi. I guess I have to buy my own drink.

100
00:11:24.785 --> 00:11:26.014
I'm sorry. one cola.

101
00:11:26.313 --> 00:11:27.385
Charles here was just telling me that I'm

102
00:11:27.386 --> 00:11:29.627
like one of the first sea creatures that grew legs.

103
00:11:29.628 --> 00:11:31.007
Tiny bit sexier.

104
00:11:31.574 --> 00:11:33.460
I'm sorry. this is my sister. Raven.

105
00:11:34.509 --> 00:11:37.604
-Hi. Amy.
-And what do you study?

106
00:11:37.605 --> 00:11:40.045
- Waitressing.
- Aah.

107
00:11:43.026 --> 00:11:44.817
Oh look. you have hetero-chromia too!

108
00:11:44.902 --> 00:11:47.131
- Say. what?
- Look at her eye..

109
00:11:49.950 --> 00:11:52.602
Right. Raven get your coat please.

110
00:11:53.667 --> 00:11:55.252
Charles: Don't talk to me. you did
that on purpose.

111
00:11:55.378 --> 00:11:56.640
- I did not!
- Yes you did!

112
00:11:56.735 --> 00:11:59.239
Why would I do it on purpose?
You know I can't control it sometimes.

113
00:11:59.348 --> 00:12:02.411
- When I'm stressed or tired..
- You seem to be doing a perfectly
good job right now.

114
00:12:03.024 --> 00:12:04.915
"Mutant and proud"

115
00:12:05.022 --> 00:12:08.514
Why is it always the pretty mutations.
or invisible ones like yours.

116
00:12:08.639 --> 00:12:10.198
If you're a freak. better hide.

117
00:12:10.309 --> 00:12:12.203
You're being ridiculous!

118
00:12:12.325 --> 00:12:14.643
Look. I don't mean to
sound like an old fart.

119
00:12:14.735 --> 00:12:19.318
- Which you are.
- Sometimes. but we've talked about this. Raven.

120
00:12:19.836 --> 00:12:23.950
A small slip up is one thing.
A big one does not bear thinking about.

121
00:12:29.514 --> 00:12:31.840
"Mutant and proud"

122
00:12:34.358 --> 00:12:36.187
"Mutant and proud"?

123
00:12:47.206 --> 00:12:49.037
If only...

124
00:12:54.602 --> 00:12:56.950
- Would you date me?
- Of course I would.

125
00:12:57.139 --> 00:12:58.996
Any young man would be lucky to have you.

126
00:12:59.089 --> 00:13:01.379
- You're stunning!
- Looking like this?

127
00:13:01.500 --> 00:13:03.359
Like. you...what?

128
00:13:06.960 --> 00:13:08.082
Blue?

129
00:13:10.865 --> 00:13:13.682
- You're my oldest friend.
- I'm your only friend.

130
00:13:13.949 --> 00:13:15.604
Thank you for that.

131
00:13:15.988 --> 00:13:17.024
Well?

132
00:13:17.194 --> 00:13:21.023
I'm incapable of thinking of you that way.
You...I feel responsible for you.

133
00:13:21.157 --> 00:13:24.221
Anything else would just feel...wrong.

134
00:13:24.529 --> 00:13:27.107
- But what if you didn't know me?
- Unfortunately I do know you.

135
00:13:27.218 --> 00:13:30.533
I don't know what's got into you lately?
You're awfully concerned with your looks.

136
00:13:35.318 --> 00:13:37.374
I'm sleepy.
Will you read to me?

137
00:13:37.375 --> 00:13:39.894
I can't. I have my thesis coming up. I have to study.

138
00:13:39.895 --> 00:13:42.795
Well fine. read about your thesis
it always sends me right off.

139
00:13:42.796 --> 00:13:46.653
To Homo neanderthalensis.
his  mutant cousin Homo sapiens.

140
00:13:46.654 --> 00:13:48.471
was an aberration.

141
00:13:48.582 --> 00:13:51.551
<i>Peaceful co-habitation. if ever it existed.</i>

142
00:13:51.552 --> 00:13:53.037
<i>was short lived.</i>

143
00:13:53.353 --> 00:13:57.574
<i>Records show. without exception that the
arrival of the mutated human species</i>

144
00:13:57.575 --> 00:14:02.660
<i>in any region was followed by the immediate
extinction of their less evolved kin.</i>

145
00:14:09.025 --> 00:14:11.858
Possession of this gold is illegal.

146
00:14:12.083 --> 00:14:13.914
I should inform the police.

147
00:14:14.242 --> 00:14:15.964
Let's not play this game.

148
00:14:16.130 --> 00:14:18.048
Where did you get it?

149
00:14:18.706 --> 00:14:20.089
A friend.

150
00:14:20.090 --> 00:14:22.446
He recommended your bank. most highly.

151
00:14:24.581 --> 00:14:25.624
I see.

152
00:14:25.793 --> 00:14:27.777
Do you know our terms. sir?

153
00:14:28.424 --> 00:14:29.467
Yes.

154
00:14:30.727 --> 00:14:33.195
And you should know mine.

155
00:14:35.730 --> 00:14:38.872
This gold is what remains of my people.

156
00:14:39.681 --> 00:14:42.665
Melted from their possessions.

157
00:14:43.255 --> 00:14:45.372
Torn from their teeth.

158
00:14:45.578 --> 00:14:48.740
And you're going to help me find
the bastards responsible for it.

159
00:14:53.945 --> 00:14:55.730
Don't touch that alarm.

160
00:14:58.194 --> 00:14:59.322
I want Schmidt.

161
00:15:01.097 --> 00:15:02.471
Klaus Schmidt.

162
00:15:02.730 --> 00:15:03.772
Where is he?

163
00:15:03.897 --> 00:15:06.227
Out clients don't provide addresses.
We're  not...

164
00:15:06.228 --> 00:15:08.082
Not that sort of bank?

165
00:15:16.645 --> 00:15:17.946
Metal fillings. eh?

166
00:15:17.947 --> 00:15:18.999
Not gold.

167
00:15:19.000 --> 00:15:21.262
Worried someone might steal them?

168
00:15:21.263 --> 00:15:25.078
Argentina!
Schmidt is in Argentina!

169
00:15:25.838 --> 00:15:28.651
Villa Gesell.
Please. please!

170
00:15:45.263 --> 00:15:46.306
Thank you.

171
00:15:50.930 --> 00:15:53.471
I would love to kill you.

172
00:15:57.392 --> 00:15:59.374
So. mark my words.

173
00:15:59.826 --> 00:16:02.757
If you warn anyone I'm coming.

174
00:16:04.299 --> 00:16:05.712
I will find you.

175
00:16:09.331 --> 00:16:13.310
Las Vegas. Nevada

176
00:16:18.088 --> 00:16:20.362
Another day at the office.

177
00:16:21.210 --> 00:16:22.782
 Is that Colonel Hendry?

178
00:16:23.176 --> 00:16:25.397
- The NATO guy?
- Yeah.

179
00:16:26.633 --> 00:16:27.990
Yes it is.

180
00:16:28.270 --> 00:16:29.618
'Cause that's three mob bosses..

181
00:16:29.745 --> 00:16:32.712
the Italian ambassador
and the CEO of Lockheed.

182
00:16:33.010 --> 00:16:37.405
They can't all be communists.
This Hellfire club's gotta be something else.

183
00:16:38.796 --> 00:16:43.198
Do you see that?
Hello. girls!

184
00:16:43.599 --> 00:16:46.055
Wow. very nice.

185
00:16:47.134 --> 00:16:48.637
Wha...what are you doing?

186
00:16:48.774 --> 00:16:51.426
Here's things that the CIA didn't give me.

187
00:16:51.622 --> 00:16:52.744
Stay put.

188
00:16:55.677 --> 00:16:57.583
- Colonel Hendry?
- Yes. ma'am.

189
00:16:57.708 --> 00:17:00.738
Emma Frost.
Sebastian Shaw's associate.

190
00:17:01.696 --> 00:17:04.005
And where is. Mr. Shaw?

191
00:17:04.119 --> 00:17:08.584
We're having a party. and here's the entertainment.
Come with me.

192
00:17:09.071 --> 00:17:10.114
(Palisades Park by Freddy Cannon )

193
00:17:10.115 --> 00:17:13.041
*Down. like a roller coaster*

194
00:17:13.042 --> 00:17:14.444
*Back like a loop-the-loop*

195
00:17:14.445 --> 00:17:17.830
*And around like a merry-go-round*

196
00:17:17.831 --> 00:17:20.333
*We ate and ate at a hot dog stand*

197
00:17:20.334 --> 00:17:23.136
*We danced around to a rockin' band*

198
00:17:23.137 --> 00:17:26.843
*And when I could. I gave that girl a hug*

199
00:17:26.844 --> 00:17:29.386
*In the tunnel of love*

200
00:17:29.387 --> 00:17:31.738
*You'll never know how great a kiss can feel*

201
00:17:31.739 --> 00:17:34.413
*When you stop at the top of a Ferris wheel*

202
00:17:34.414 --> 00:17:38.753
*When I fell in love. down at Palisades Park*

203
00:17:47.754 --> 00:17:49.339
Hello beautiful. how are you?

204
00:17:49.428 --> 00:17:51.742
Hey baby. you want to find a quiet place?

205
00:17:51.891 --> 00:17:55.278
I'm so sorry.
I've been booked by Colonel Hendry.

206
00:17:57.470 --> 00:17:58.924
Excuse me.

207
00:17:58.925 --> 00:18:00.314
*We ate and ate at a hot dog stand*

208
00:18:00.315 --> 00:18:03.349
*We danced around to a rockin' band*

209
00:18:03.350 --> 00:18:07.192
*And when I could. I gave that girl a hug*

210
00:18:07.193 --> 00:18:09.510
*In the tunnel of love*

211
00:18:09.511 --> 00:18:11.782
*You'll never know how great a kiss can feel*

212
00:18:11.783 --> 00:18:12.809
*When you stop at the....*

213
00:18:19.440 --> 00:18:22.753
- Are you sure we can't get you a refill. Bob?
- Bob: No.

214
00:18:23.351 --> 00:18:28.411
So. I hear you blocked the proposal to position
Jupiter missiles in Turkey.

215
00:18:30.465 --> 00:18:34.515
- I expect you'll reconsider.
- Bob: We've had this conversation.

216
00:18:34.642 --> 00:18:38.505
You put our nukes in Turkey.
or anywhere that close to Russia.

217
00:18:38.653 --> 00:18:42.225
and you're looking at war.
Nuclear war.

218
00:19:15.162 --> 00:19:18.900
I don't ask for favors. Colonel.
I express my expectations.

219
00:19:19.093 --> 00:19:26.944
So. let me say it again.
I expect you'll reconsider.

220
00:19:26.947 --> 00:19:32.802
The only thing I will reconsider.
is having another glass of that delicious champagne.

221
00:19:44.573 --> 00:19:48.035
Bob: What the hell did you put in my drink?

222
00:20:05.377 --> 00:20:09.972
<i>**You're thinking of running. hiding?
We'd find you. Hendry.**</i>

223
00:20:10.229 --> 00:20:13.130
<i>**There's not a fortress in the world
that could keep us out.**</i>

224
00:20:29.934 --> 00:20:33.011
Shaw: Magnificent. isn't she. Bob?

225
00:20:33.950 --> 00:20:37.544
Genetic mutation. the evolution of a human genome.

226
00:20:38.239 --> 00:20:39.532
Where's Azazel?

227
00:20:45.976 --> 00:20:47.618
Ah. we don't want
the Colonel to be late.

228
00:20:51.611 --> 00:20:53.047
Come here.

229
00:20:55.667 --> 00:20:58.647
Missiles in Turkey send a very clear message.

230
00:20:58.648 --> 00:21:00.035
We ever decided to fire them.

231
00:21:00.037 --> 00:21:02.703
the Russian early warning system won't
even have time to kick in.

232
00:21:02.704 --> 00:21:04.345
McCone: This better be important. MacTaggert

233
00:21:04.360 --> 00:21:05.896
Whoa. whoa. whoa. slow down.

234
00:21:06.397 --> 00:21:09.161
You smoking them funny cigarettes?
People don't disappear.

235
00:21:09.305 --> 00:21:12.320
Colonel Hendry was there.
He was there McCone. in the Hellfire club.

236
00:21:12.446 --> 00:21:13.947
Colonel Hendry?

237
00:21:14.119 --> 00:21:17.892
I agree with you. General.
I've reconsidered my position.

238
00:21:17.999 --> 00:21:21.194
And I now believe that we should put
Jupiter Missiles in Turkey.

239
00:21:21.360 --> 00:21:22.350
Colonel Hendry is here.

240
00:21:22.472 --> 00:21:26.199
So. unless he magically traveled
3.000 miles in the last ten minutes.

241
00:21:26.200 --> 00:21:29.170
Listen to me. I suggest that you stop
wasting my time.

242
00:21:29.343 --> 00:21:32.092
Looks like Hendry wants to start
World War III.

243
00:21:32.093 --> 00:21:33.995
I have better things to deal with right now. MacTaggert.

244
00:21:34.347 --> 00:21:35.542
Sir. I...!

245
00:21:37.185 --> 00:21:38.422
Have you lost your mind?

246
00:21:38.993 --> 00:21:40.917
So. now what?

247
00:21:42.392 --> 00:21:45.005
We find an expert on Genetic Mutation.

248
00:21:45.777 --> 00:21:49.976
<i>Professor of genetics.
Charles Francis Xavier.</i>

249
00:21:52.621 --> 00:21:54.795
So. how does it feel to be a professor?

250
00:21:54.796 --> 00:21:58.313
Well. don't call me that. You don't get to be called a
Professor until you actually have a teaching position.

251
00:21:58.468 --> 00:22:01.581
- I know. but it suits you.
- No. don't say that. do say
"Lets go have a drink".

252
00:22:01.708 --> 00:22:03.510
- Let's go have a drink.
- Charles: Wonderful!

253
00:22:16.714 --> 00:22:19.804
Villa Gesell. Argentina

254
00:22:31.641 --> 00:22:34.549
- Good evening. my friends!
- Good evening!

255
00:22:34.550 --> 00:22:35.825
- Hot. no?
- Yes...

256
00:22:35.826 --> 00:22:37.769
One beer. please.

257
00:23:01.436 --> 00:23:02.673
German beer.

258
00:23:02.927 --> 00:23:03.969
Of course.

259
00:23:03.970 --> 00:23:07.769
Yes. it's Bitburger.
You like it?

260
00:23:14.054 --> 00:23:15.436
The best.

261
00:23:20.739 --> 00:23:22.936
What brings you to Argentina?

262
00:23:25.036 --> 00:23:28.571
The climate. I'm a pig farmer.

263
00:23:32.684 --> 00:23:35.662
Tailor. since I was a boy.

264
00:23:36.127 --> 00:23:38.692
My father made the finest
suits in Düsseldorf.

265
00:23:39.550 --> 00:23:41.882
My parents were from Düsseldorf.

266
00:23:41.886 --> 00:23:43.453
- Ah.
- Yeah.

267
00:23:43.810 --> 00:23:45.031
What was their name?

268
00:23:45.329 --> 00:23:46.870
They didn't have a name.

269
00:23:48.726 --> 00:23:50.588
It was taken away from them.

270
00:23:51.049 --> 00:23:52.445
By pig farmers....

271
00:23:53.712 --> 00:23:55.013
...and tailors.

272
00:24:24.076 --> 00:24:25.822
Blood and honor.

273
00:24:25.896 --> 00:24:27.983
Which would you care to shed first?

274
00:24:28.188 --> 00:24:30.187
We were under orders.

275
00:24:30.188 --> 00:24:31.310
Blood then.

276
00:24:34.016 --> 00:24:35.130
Freeze. asshole.

277
00:24:35.567 --> 00:24:37.061
Come on. shoot.

278
00:24:57.263 --> 00:24:59.649
Who...what are you?

279
00:25:02.230 --> 00:25:04.710
Let's just say I'm Frankenstein's monster.

280
00:25:17.145 --> 00:25:19.054
I'm looking for my creator.

281
00:25:24.078 --> 00:25:29.951
Drink. drink. drink!

282
00:25:41.720 --> 00:25:43.696
Oh. I'm so proud of  you.

283
00:25:44.776 --> 00:25:47.686
I need another drink. and you
need another cola.

284
00:25:51.775 --> 00:25:55.482
- Congratulations. Professor!
- Thank you very much. it's much harder than it looks. actually..

285
00:25:55.596 --> 00:25:58.082
- No. on your presentation.
- You knew my presentation?

286
00:25:58.190 --> 00:25:59.533
How nice of you. thank you very much.

287
00:25:59.658 --> 00:26:01.293
- Moira MacTaggert.
- Charles Xavier.

288
00:26:01.294 --> 00:26:02.061
Do you have a minute?

289
00:26:02.328 --> 00:26:06.597
For a pretty little beam with a
mutated MCR-1 gene. I have five.

290
00:26:07.028 --> 00:26:11.337
I say. MCR-1. you would say.
golden hair.

291
00:26:11.486 --> 00:26:15.102
It's a mutation. it's a very groovy mutation.

292
00:26:15.239 --> 00:26:19.789
Mutation you know. took us from single
celled organisms.

293
00:26:19.945 --> 00:26:21.716
to the dominate form...

294
00:26:21.822 --> 00:26:25.989
You know what. this routine may go over great
with the co-eds. but I'm here on business.

295
00:26:26.315 --> 00:26:28.752
- What?
- I really need your help.

296
00:26:29.492 --> 00:26:30.823
All right.

297
00:26:30.931 --> 00:26:34.277
The kind of mutations that you were
talking about in your thesis.

298
00:26:34.435 --> 00:26:36.877
I need to know if they may have already happened.

299
00:26:38.145 --> 00:26:40.096
In people alive today.

300
00:26:51.436 --> 00:26:52.702
Professor?

301
00:26:54.845 --> 00:26:56.332
I think we should just talk when you're sober.

302
00:26:56.438 --> 00:26:57.832
Do you have any time tomorrow?

303
00:26:59.400 --> 00:27:03.337
Something tells me. you already know
the answer to your question.

304
00:27:05.370 --> 00:27:06.745
This is very important to me.

305
00:27:06.842 --> 00:27:09.451
And if I can help you. I will do my utmost.

306
00:27:10.327 --> 00:27:11.204
Thank you.

307
00:27:11.465 --> 00:27:14.578
Miami. Florida

308
00:27:14.844 --> 00:27:18.494
- Still drinking champagne. Bob?
- Bob: I will pass.

309
00:27:19.259 --> 00:27:22.230
Okay. well so much for the pleasantries.

310
00:27:22.777 --> 00:27:26.222
I was wondering. who you told
about our little arrangement?

311
00:27:26.628 --> 00:27:27.908
No one.

312
00:27:30.442 --> 00:27:32.636
- He's telling the truth.
- Shaw: Good.

313
00:27:32.740 --> 00:27:36.807
Well I guess we're done here.
Let's wrap things up. shall we?

314
00:27:40.843 --> 00:27:43.529
Well I knew better than to trust you.

315
00:27:44.314 --> 00:27:47.771
Now you let me walk out of here
with my money.

316
00:27:47.772 --> 00:27:51.830
Or I will pull this pin and we all die.

317
00:27:52.727 --> 00:27:55.709
Go ahead. pull it.

318
00:27:55.710 --> 00:27:57.374
I'll do it. I swear to god.

319
00:28:07.197 --> 00:28:08.601
No you won't.

320
00:28:13.748 --> 00:28:15.046
But I will.

321
00:28:28.250 --> 00:28:29.449
You're one of them?

322
00:28:29.558 --> 00:28:33.391
Shaw: Very astute of you. Colonel Hendry.
You want to guess what I can do?

323
00:28:33.507 --> 00:28:36.408
I've got the power to absorb energy.
It keeps me young.

324
00:28:36.565 --> 00:28:38.040
That's the boring part.

325
00:28:38.201 --> 00:28:41.819
The fun stuff is what I can do with it
once I got it.

326
00:28:48.160 --> 00:28:50.115
CIA HEADQUARTERS. LANGLEY. VIRGINIA
The advent of the nuclear age.
may have accelerated the mutation process.

327
00:28:50.116 --> 00:28:52.510
may have accelerated the mutation process.

328
00:28:52.511 --> 00:28:57.458
Individual's with extraordinary abilities may
already be among us.

329
00:28:58.217 --> 00:28:59.325
Thank you very much.

330
00:28:59.326 --> 00:29:02.072
MacTaggert. you really think that some crackpot scientist.

331
00:29:02.073 --> 00:29:05.673
is going to make me believe in sparkly dames
and vanishing men?

332
00:29:05.799 --> 00:29:08.549
You just brought yourself a one way ticket
back to the typing pool.

333
00:29:08.796 --> 00:29:10.275
This meeting is over.

334
00:29:10.407 --> 00:29:12.822
Uh. please sit down agent. MacTaggert.

335
00:29:13.787 --> 00:29:16.334
I didn't really expect you to believe me.

336
00:29:16.335 --> 00:29:18.240
Given that all you could think about during my presentation.

337
00:29:18.364 --> 00:29:20.945
was what sort of pie they were serving in the commissary.

338
00:29:22.023 --> 00:29:23.882
It's apple pecan.

339
00:29:24.179 --> 00:29:26.512
I haven't been entirely honest with you. luv. I'm sorry.

340
00:29:26.620 --> 00:29:30.564
You see. one of the many spectacular things my
mutation allows me to do.

341
00:29:30.565 --> 00:29:32.558
Is that I can read your  mind.

342
00:29:33.028 --> 00:29:34.622
I've seen this before in a magic show.

343
00:29:34.774 --> 00:29:38.557
Are you going to ask us to think of a number
between one and ten now?

344
00:29:39.420 --> 00:29:40.341
No. Agent Stryker.

345
00:29:40.464 --> 00:29:43.845
Although I could ask  you about your son William who
you were thinking about.

346
00:29:43.953 --> 00:29:45.205
which is very nice.

347
00:29:45.336 --> 00:29:47.399
But I think I'd rather ask you
about the Jupiter...

348
00:29:47.535 --> 00:29:50.145
...missiles America are currently placing in Turkey.

349
00:29:51.992 --> 00:29:54.718
He's a goddamn spy!
You brought a goddamn spy!

350
00:29:54.823 --> 00:29:56.762
I did not. I would never bring one here!

351
00:30:15.802 --> 00:30:17.509
How's that for a magic trick?

352
00:30:20.649 --> 00:30:22.982
Best I've ever seen.

353
00:30:23.591 --> 00:30:25.059
I want them out of here.

354
00:30:25.218 --> 00:30:28.374
And lock down until I can figure out
what to do.

355
00:30:29.328 --> 00:30:33.632
My facility is off site. I'll take them.

356
00:30:35.289 --> 00:30:36.078
I can't believe this.

357
00:30:36.183 --> 00:30:38.642
You'd think the director of the CIA
would have a little more composure.

358
00:30:38.762 --> 00:30:40.144
We should be going after Shaw right now. but...

359
00:30:40.255 --> 00:30:42.266
...instead he's up there worrying about the wrong mutants.

360
00:30:42.515 --> 00:30:43.601
What are we doing to do. Lavene?

361
00:30:44.232 --> 00:30:47.215
Lavene?
Lavene. what's wrong with you?

362
00:30:49.600 --> 00:30:53.451
<i>**Absolutely nothing. I've just frozen him for the
moment because I'd like to talk to you.**</i>

363
00:30:53.536 --> 00:30:54.741
<i>**It's good. isn't it?**</i>

364
00:30:54.742 --> 00:30:57.652
<i>**I'm as interested in this.
Sebastian Shaw as you are.**</i>

365
00:30:57.653 --> 00:31:00.773
<i>**...and if you still want my help. meet me on
the third floor of the parking garage.**</i>

366
00:31:02.051 --> 00:31:04.768
I've always known that
there were people like you out there.

367
00:31:04.895 --> 00:31:08.397
I've been the laughing stock of this agency
for years but I knew it.

368
00:31:08.488 --> 00:31:09.570
You're going to love my facility.

369
00:31:09.682 --> 00:31:11.462
- That's going to have to wait.
- Man in Black: Why?

370
00:31:11.606 --> 00:31:13.492
Agent MacTaggert has to lead us to Sebastian Shaw.

371
00:31:13.618 --> 00:31:15.917
and if we don't move now apparently
we're going to loose him.

372
00:31:16.090 --> 00:31:16.795
What?

373
00:31:16.908 --> 00:31:20.077
Not only can he read minds.
he can communicate with them as well.

374
00:31:20.171 --> 00:31:21.990
Moria and I have just had a lovely conversation.

375
00:31:22.096 --> 00:31:24.022
- Yes. we did.
- That is incredible!

376
00:31:25.336 --> 00:31:28.591
But I cannot take you anywhere else.
without permission from upstairs.

377
00:31:28.683 --> 00:31:30.850
- Would you like to see one more magic trick?
- Okay.

378
00:31:30.950 --> 00:31:32.546
- Get in the car.
- Good idea.

379
00:31:53.820 --> 00:31:55.093
Herr Doctor...

380
00:31:59.379 --> 00:32:01.483
Little Erik Lehnsherr.

381
00:32:01.719 --> 00:32:03.202
He's here to kill you.

382
00:32:10.233 --> 00:32:12.943
What kind of greeting is that?

383
00:32:15.244 --> 00:32:17.124
...after all these years.

384
00:32:26.811 --> 00:32:29.279
Emma... 

385
00:32:29.280 --> 00:32:31.332
We don't harm our own kind.

386
00:32:33.176 --> 00:32:35.471
Ah. now it's a party.

387
00:32:36.523 --> 00:32:41.153
This is the US Coast guard.
Do not attempt to move your vessel.

388
00:32:41.288 --> 00:32:43.087
Stay where you are.

389
00:32:49.253 --> 00:32:50.597
They have a telepath.

390
00:32:54.602 --> 00:32:55.906
I've lost. Shaw!

391
00:32:56.226 --> 00:32:57.947
I've lost. I've lost. Shaw.

392
00:32:57.948 --> 00:33:00.857
There. there's something blocking me.
This has never happened to me before.

393
00:33:00.858 --> 00:33:02.668
I think there's someone like
me on that ship.

394
00:33:02.825 --> 00:33:05.608
- Like you?
- I'm sorry. a telepath.

395
00:33:06.284 --> 00:33:08.744
This is incredible. I can actually feel
her inside my mind.

396
00:33:08.750 --> 00:33:10.681
I'm very sorry. but I don't think I'm
going to be much help to you tonight.

397
00:33:10.788 --> 00:33:11.788
You're on your own.

398
00:33:25.549 --> 00:33:27.055
- Oh my god.
- Moria: Jesus.

399
00:33:30.580 --> 00:33:31.565
Man in Black: Get inside.

400
00:33:37.807 --> 00:33:39.135
Stop. stop. stop!

401
00:33:39.929 --> 00:33:42.871
Charles!
You okay?

402
00:33:42.980 --> 00:33:44.492
There's someone else out there.

403
00:33:48.433 --> 00:33:49.725
There!

404
00:33:52.632 --> 00:33:53.825
Time to go.

405
00:34:49.045 --> 00:34:50.438
Charles: Let go!

406
00:34:52.334 --> 00:34:53.803
Charles: You got to let it go!

407
00:34:53.908 --> 00:34:55.711
You've got help him...there's
someone in the water. help him!

408
00:34:55.802 --> 00:34:59.261
Let it go!
You have to let it go!

409
00:35:19.088 --> 00:35:22.485
<i>**You can't. you'll drown.
You have to let go.**</i>

410
00:35:22.576 --> 00:35:25.313
<i>**I know what this means to you
but you're going to die.**</i>

411
00:35:25.594 --> 00:35:29.644
<i>**Please. Erik. calm your mind.**</i>

412
00:35:41.082 --> 00:35:42.615
Get off of me. get off!

413
00:35:42.724 --> 00:35:44.929
Calm down. please.
We're here!

414
00:35:45.078 --> 00:35:47.074
- Who are you?
-  My name's Charles Xavier.

415
00:35:47.196 --> 00:35:49.077
You were in my head.

416
00:35:49.355 --> 00:35:50.701
How did you do that?

417
00:35:50.808 --> 00:35:52.124
You have your tricks. I have mine.

418
00:35:52.234 --> 00:35:54.658
I'm like you. just calm your mind.

419
00:35:57.025 --> 00:36:00.890
- I thought I was alone.
- You're not alone.

420
00:36:02.407 --> 00:36:05.720
Erik. you're not alone.

421
00:36:08.545 --> 00:36:12.122
Covert CIA Research Base

422
00:36:26.093 --> 00:36:28.109
Man in Black: Welcome to my facility.

423
00:36:28.990 --> 00:36:30.519
My mission has been to investigate the

424
00:36:30.634 --> 00:36:34.120
application of paranormal powers
for military defense.

425
00:36:34.225 --> 00:36:35.523
Or offense.

426
00:36:35.820 --> 00:36:38.936
This guy. Shaw. Schmidt. whatever
you want to call him.

427
00:36:39.072 --> 00:36:40.752
He's working with the Russians.

428
00:36:40.877 --> 00:36:42.435
We might need your help to stop him.

429
00:36:42.549 --> 00:36:43.440
Marvelous.

430
00:36:43.565 --> 00:36:46.268
So we're to be the CIA's new
mutant division. yes?

431
00:36:47.449 --> 00:36:48.665
Something like that.

432
00:36:52.333 --> 00:36:56.595
Hank: It's a supersonic. The most
advanced plane ever built.

433
00:36:57.898 --> 00:37:00.965
You should see it in real life.
It's incredible.

434
00:37:01.075 --> 00:37:04.940
Hank. these are the special new recruits I
was telling you about.

435
00:37:05.046 --> 00:37:06.030
This is. Hank McCoy.

436
00:37:06.159 --> 00:37:08.132
One of our most talented young researchers.

437
00:37:08.235 --> 00:37:11.831
How wonderful. another mutant.
Already here.

438
00:37:11.946 --> 00:37:14.649
- Why didn't you say?
- Say what?

439
00:37:15.910 --> 00:37:17.504
Because you don't know.

440
00:37:18.305 --> 00:37:21.402
I am so. so terribly sorry!

441
00:37:24.106 --> 00:37:25.229
Hank?

442
00:37:25.354 --> 00:37:27.326
You didn't ask. so I didn't tell.

443
00:37:27.858 --> 00:37:31.253
So  your mutation's what?
You're super smart?

444
00:37:31.396 --> 00:37:34.598
I'll say. Hank here graduated
honors at the age of fifteen.

445
00:37:35.385 --> 00:37:37.508
I wish that's all it was.

446
00:37:37.694 --> 00:37:41.234
You're among friends now. Hank.
You could show off.

447
00:37:57.232 --> 00:37:58.469
Splendid.

448
00:38:04.209 --> 00:38:06.414
- Sorry.
- Yes. yes.

449
00:38:20.830 --> 00:38:23.991
- You're amazing.
- Really?

450
00:38:29.324 --> 00:38:32.769
<i>The presence of U.S. missiles in Turkey
represents an unprecedented threat</i>

451
00:38:32.860 --> 00:38:34.549
<i>to the people of the Soviet Union.</i>

452
00:38:34.672 --> 00:38:38.335
<i>Warned Russian Mister Gromeko. earlier today</i>

453
00:38:38.565 --> 00:38:43.825
<i>But he was quick to insist the Russians
would not be the first to initiate any military action.</i>

454
00:38:43.995 --> 00:38:46.277
Yeah. we'll fix that as soon as
we get to Russia.

455
00:38:46.933 --> 00:38:51.089
- Unless the CIA finds us first.
- I'll take care of them too.

456
00:38:52.336 --> 00:38:57.388
If that telepath gets inside your head.
he won't be as much fun as I am.

457
00:38:57.826 --> 00:38:59.784
Already in hand. my love.

458
00:39:09.463 --> 00:39:10.921
The Russians...

459
00:39:13.311 --> 00:39:14.797
...made me this.

460
00:39:18.187 --> 00:39:20.802
So. what am I thinking?

461
00:39:30.278 --> 00:39:31.718
I don't know.

462
00:39:34.487 --> 00:39:38.425
I was thinking that you are the most exquisite
thing I've ever seen in my life.

463
00:39:42.543 --> 00:39:44.991
And that this needs ice.

464
00:39:45.986 --> 00:39:47.282
Shaw: Fetch me some.

465
00:39:47.373 --> 00:39:48.761
There's a good girl.

466
00:40:14.402 --> 00:40:18.605
I...I promised myself I'd find a cure.
Ever since I was a little boy.

467
00:40:18.703 --> 00:40:22.474
You have no idea what I'd give to feel...

468
00:40:23.020 --> 00:40:24.810
- ...normal.
- Normal.

469
00:40:29.346 --> 00:40:31.648
Charles has never understood.

470
00:40:31.958 --> 00:40:35.303
He's different. but he's never had to hide.

471
00:40:36.040 --> 00:40:40.250
Hank this serum that you're making.
it doesn't affect abilities. right?

472
00:40:40.303 --> 00:40:43.056
Just appearance.
Normalizes it.

473
00:40:43.183 --> 00:40:44.367
Yeah.

474
00:40:45.169 --> 00:40:46.917
Do you think it would work on me?

475
00:40:48.247 --> 00:40:50.604
I can look into it. if you'd like.

476
00:40:50.605 --> 00:40:54.227
That's the least I can do after asking you to
come down here with such a weird request.

477
00:40:54.399 --> 00:40:55.122
I have to admit.

478
00:40:55.212 --> 00:40:57.887
usually when guys ask me out they're
not after my blood.

479
00:40:58.578 --> 00:41:04.470
S..sorry. I didn't intend to be forward.
I was just...I was excited.

480
00:41:04.600 --> 00:41:06.740
You know. the nature of your mutation.

481
00:41:06.863 --> 00:41:10.064
If any genes hold the key to changing appearance.
it's yours.

482
00:41:10.168 --> 00:41:14.621
Hank. you aren't being forward.
that's kinda what I meant.

483
00:41:15.091 --> 00:41:20.634
- No. but I'm just sorry if you thought I was.
- And I'm sorry that you weren't.

484
00:41:22.125 --> 00:41:24.595
Go ahead. take the blood.

485
00:41:36.451 --> 00:41:38.250
Sorry. did I hurt you?

486
00:41:40.736 --> 00:41:41.879
Kinky!

487
00:41:43.830 --> 00:41:49.611
By the way. if I looked like you.
I wouldn't change a thing.

488
00:42:16.181 --> 00:42:20.395
Charles: What I know about you. I'm surprised
you've managed to stay this long.

489
00:42:21.887 --> 00:42:25.390
- What do you know about me?
- Everything.

490
00:42:25.627 --> 00:42:27.659
Then you know to stay out of my head.

491
00:42:27.782 --> 00:42:31.303
I'm sorry Erik. but I've seen what
Shaw did to you.

492
00:42:32.833 --> 00:42:35.224
I felt your agony.

493
00:42:37.446 --> 00:42:39.290
I can help you.

494
00:42:45.870 --> 00:42:47.321
I don't need your help.

495
00:42:47.434 --> 00:42:49.546
Charles: Don't kid yourself.
You needed my help last night.

496
00:42:49.654 --> 00:42:51.831
It's not just me you're walking away from.

497
00:42:52.560 --> 00:42:56.705
Here you have the chance to be part of
something much bigger than yourself.

498
00:42:59.270 --> 00:43:02.232
I won't stop you leaving. I could.

499
00:43:05.495 --> 00:43:06.839
But I won't.

500
00:43:10.875 --> 00:43:12.423
Shaw's got friends.

501
00:43:13.128 --> 00:43:14.777
You could do with some.

502
00:43:20.915 --> 00:43:23.875
Hank turned that
radar installation into a transmitter.

503
00:43:23.984 --> 00:43:26.112
It's designed to amplify brain waves.

504
00:43:26.252 --> 00:43:28.645
...so it could enhance your telepathic powers.

505
00:43:28.814 --> 00:43:31.237
Help us find other mutants for our division.

506
00:43:31.331 --> 00:43:33.353
What if they don't want to be found by you?

507
00:43:33.461 --> 00:43:34.961
Erik.

508
00:43:35.397 --> 00:43:36.963
You decided to stay.

509
00:43:39.487 --> 00:43:43.267
If a new species is being discovered.
it should be by its own kind.

510
00:43:43.530 --> 00:43:46.235
Charles and I find the mutants.
no suits.

511
00:43:46.391 --> 00:43:48.050
First of all. that's my machine out there.

512
00:43:48.190 --> 00:43:49.427
Second of all. and much more importantly.

513
00:43:49.541 --> 00:43:51.120
this is Charles' decision.

514
00:43:51.225 --> 00:43:54.092
Charles is fine with the CIA being involved.
Isn't that right?

515
00:43:55.869 --> 00:43:59.939
No. I'm sorry but. I'm with Erik.

516
00:44:00.013 --> 00:44:02.484
We'll find them alone.

517
00:44:03.994 --> 00:44:05.307
What if I say no?

518
00:44:06.488 --> 00:44:09.355
Then good luck using your installation without me.

519
00:44:21.756 --> 00:44:24.107
I call it. Cerebro.

520
00:44:25.682 --> 00:44:27.760
- Isn't that Spanish for "brain"?
- Yes.

521
00:44:28.294 --> 00:44:31.749
Okay so. the electrodes connect
Charles to the transmitter on the roof.

522
00:44:31.750 --> 00:44:33.642
And picks up a mutant.

523
00:44:33.766 --> 00:44:35.865
His brain sends a signal through a relay.

524
00:44:36.002 --> 00:44:38.552
And then the co-ordinates of their
location are printed out here.

525
00:44:38.916 --> 00:44:41.851
- You designed this?
- Yeah.

526
00:44:45.019 --> 00:44:48.023
- What an adorable lab rat you make. Charles.
- Don't spoil this for me. Erik.

527
00:44:49.015 --> 00:44:51.666
I've been a lab rat. I know one when I see one.

528
00:44:51.778 --> 00:44:53.828
Okay. right...

529
00:44:54.325 --> 00:44:57.035
- Are you sure we can't shave your head?
- Don't touch my hair.

530
00:45:41.542 --> 00:45:42.621
It's working!

531
00:45:49.185 --> 00:45:52.595
*60's dance music*

532
00:46:00.663 --> 00:46:03.496
With that Daddy-O. you get a private dance.

533
00:46:06.563 --> 00:46:09.631
You cat's know it's double for both. right?

534
00:46:10.431 --> 00:46:12.788
No. that won't be necessary.
although I'm sure we...

535
00:46:12.896 --> 00:46:15.463
We were thinking. we'll show you ours.

536
00:46:15.649 --> 00:46:17.513
...if you show us yours.

537
00:46:17.641 --> 00:46:19.965
Baby. that is not the way it works around here.

538
00:46:22.216 --> 00:46:25.599
- More tea. Vicar?
- Charles: Don't mind if I do.

539
00:46:28.039 --> 00:46:29.525
My turn.

540
00:46:47.432 --> 00:46:49.902
How would you like a job. where you
get to keep your clothes on?

541
00:46:55.841 --> 00:46:58.140
- Where to fellas?
- Richmond. Virginia.

542
00:46:58.246 --> 00:47:01.237
Right. so you want the airport. the station. what?

543
00:47:01.329 --> 00:47:04.250
No we were rather hoping you would
take us all the way.

544
00:47:04.251 --> 00:47:05.993
That's a six hour drive.

545
00:47:05.994 --> 00:47:07.790
That will give us plenty of time to talk.

546
00:47:12.457 --> 00:47:15.167
Prison warden: What the hell does the government want
with a guy like. Alex Summers?

547
00:47:15.336 --> 00:47:17.479
I hope you're not planning on putting him with others.

548
00:47:17.605 --> 00:47:21.248
First guy I ever met who actually
prefers solitary confinement.

549
00:47:31.371 --> 00:47:33.549
- Crazy. huh?
- Girl: What?

550
00:47:34.348 --> 00:47:36.579
You like fish. I like fish too.

551
00:47:36.580 --> 00:47:39.721
Maybe we should get a bite
some time and talk about it.

552
00:47:42.128 --> 00:47:44.142
I'd rather go out with the fish.

553
00:47:50.313 --> 00:47:51.809
These fish?

554
00:48:10.839 --> 00:48:12.931
- Excuse me I'm Erik Lehnsherr.
- Charles Xavier.

555
00:48:13.041 --> 00:48:14.605
Go fuck yourselves.

556
00:48:34.644 --> 00:48:36.979
- There's nothing on radar?
- No.

557
00:48:37.071 --> 00:48:38.713
- Sonar?
- Nyet.

558
00:48:39.962 --> 00:48:41.573
Then we have a problem.

559
00:49:00.533 --> 00:49:02.436
Beautiful. isn't it?

560
00:49:03.064 --> 00:49:07.800
The reason we exist.
We are the children of the atom. my love.

561
00:49:07.925 --> 00:49:09.599
We have a situation.

562
00:49:09.835 --> 00:49:11.623
The telepath...

563
00:49:11.727 --> 00:49:13.790
I shouldn't be able to feel him at this distance.

564
00:49:13.931 --> 00:49:16.088
It's like his reach is...

565
00:49:16.484 --> 00:49:18.266
...amplified.

566
00:49:20.452 --> 00:49:22.536
They're recruiting.

567
00:49:22.991 --> 00:49:26.195
You go on to Russia.
I'll handle him.

568
00:49:27.920 --> 00:49:29.594
I can't stop thinking
about the others out there.

569
00:49:29.595 --> 00:49:32.019
All those minds that I've touched.

570
00:49:32.979 --> 00:49:38.494
I could feel them. their isolation. their hopes.
their ambitions.

571
00:49:39.058 --> 00:49:41.875
I tell you. we've started something
incredible. Erik.

572
00:49:42.427 --> 00:49:45.032
- We can help them.
- Can we?

573
00:49:46.189 --> 00:49:49.192
Identification. that's how it starts.

574
00:49:50.662 --> 00:49:54.401
Then ends with being rounded up.
Experimented on. eliminated.

575
00:49:54.509 --> 00:49:56.139
Not this time.

576
00:49:56.245 --> 00:50:00.097
We have common enemies. Shaw and the Russians
they need us.

577
00:50:00.111 --> 00:50:01.544
For now.

578
00:50:07.244 --> 00:50:08.882
We should think of code names.

579
00:50:08.973 --> 00:50:11.180
We're government agents now.
we should have secret code names.

580
00:50:11.294 --> 00:50:15.361
- I want to be called. Mystique.
- Damn. I wanted to be called. Mystique.

581
00:50:15.474 --> 00:50:17.454
- Well tough. I called it.

582
00:50:18.964 --> 00:50:22.233
Damn right.
I'm more mysterious than you.

583
00:50:24.622 --> 00:50:28.067
- Darwin. what about you?
- Well. uh. Darwin's already a nickname.

584
00:50:28.178 --> 00:50:32.208
And you know. sort of fits.
Adapt to survive and all.

585
00:50:32.633 --> 00:50:34.072
Check this out.

586
00:50:47.775 --> 00:50:49.682
- Thank you. thank you.
- Bravo. bravo.

587
00:50:50.037 --> 00:50:53.152
- What about you?
- I'm going to be...

588
00:50:54.354 --> 00:50:55.220
...Banshee.

589
00:50:55.344 --> 00:50:57.016
Why do you want to be named
after a wailing spirit?

590
00:50:57.126 --> 00:50:58.814
Sean: You might want to cover your ears.

591
00:51:14.734 --> 00:51:15.564
Your turn.

592
00:51:15.701 --> 00:51:20.397
My uh. stage name is Angel.
Kind of fits.

593
00:51:20.503 --> 00:51:23.960
- You can fly?
-  Ah. hah. And uh...

594
00:51:33.126 --> 00:51:36.564
- What's your name?
- How about Big Foot?

595
00:51:36.707 --> 00:51:39.155
Well you know what they say
about guys with big feet?

596
00:51:39.540 --> 00:51:41.696
And uh. yours are kind of small.

597
00:51:41.697 --> 00:51:43.396
Okay. now.

598
00:51:44.188 --> 00:51:46.326
Alex. what is your gift?
What can you do?

599
00:51:46.447 --> 00:51:50.289
Uh. it's not um. I just can't do it.

600
00:51:50.290 --> 00:51:52.940
- I can't do it in here.
- Can you do it out there?

601
00:51:52.941 --> 00:51:54.315
- Why don't you just do it out there.
- Angel: Come on.

602
00:51:54.316 --> 00:51:56.720
- Come on. Alex.
- Alex! Alex!

603
00:51:56.721 --> 00:51:59.831
All chanting: Alex. Alex. Alex.

604
00:52:02.447 --> 00:52:03.870
That's the spirit.

605
00:52:04.027 --> 00:52:05.574
Get down when I tell you.

606
00:52:13.348 --> 00:52:14.631
Get back.

607
00:52:19.437 --> 00:52:20.886
Get back!

608
00:52:22.250 --> 00:52:23.546
Whatever...

609
00:52:37.343 --> 00:52:41.570
We've got Intel that Shaw is meeting with
the Russian defense chief in Moscow.

610
00:52:41.571 --> 00:52:43.460
So go ahead. say it.

611
00:52:43.772 --> 00:52:46.225
I'm not here to say "I told you so".
you know why I'm here.

612
00:52:46.725 --> 00:52:48.889
Yeah. yeah. yeah. Clearance to bring
along your mutants.

613
00:52:48.890 --> 00:52:50.778
Fight fire with fire.

614
00:52:51.495 --> 00:52:52.492
Makes sense.

615
00:52:52.600 --> 00:52:54.545
Wait. you're okay with this?

616
00:52:54.652 --> 00:52:57.451
Sending in a bunch of untrained
unauthorized freaks?

617
00:52:57.558 --> 00:53:01.581
These "Freaks" are dedicated hard working people.

618
00:53:02.959 --> 00:53:04.518
Plane leaves for Russia in an hour.

619
00:53:04.646 --> 00:53:06.598
I'm telling you these kids
are not ready for. Shaw.

620
00:53:06.712 --> 00:53:09.572
I think they're going to surprise you.
They are an exceptional bunch of young people.

621
00:53:09.664 --> 00:53:10.789
What the hell?

622
00:53:14.496 --> 00:53:16.844
*Chan Romero. The hippy hippy shake*

623
00:53:22.867 --> 00:53:24.773
Harder!

624
00:53:25.387 --> 00:53:26.430
Darwin: Harder!

625
00:53:28.668 --> 00:53:30.932
What are  you doing?

626
00:53:36.552 --> 00:53:39.151
- Who destroyed the statue?
- Hank: It was. Alex.

627
00:53:39.852 --> 00:53:43.329
No Havok! We have to call him. Havok.
That's his name now.

628
00:53:43.385 --> 00:53:46.575
And we were thinking. you should be. Professor X

629
00:53:46.731 --> 00:53:49.423
And you should be. Magneto.

630
00:53:50.805 --> 00:53:52.210
Exceptional.

631
00:53:56.596 --> 00:53:58.410
I expect more from you.

632
00:54:01.575 --> 00:54:04.790
Russian Military Retreat

633
00:54:19.300 --> 00:54:20.320
We've got a problem.

634
00:54:20.455 --> 00:54:22.961
- What?
- I'm so sorry. this wasn't on the map.

635
00:54:29.515 --> 00:54:30.997
No matter what happens. act normally.

636
00:54:31.091 --> 00:54:32.550
I'll take care of this. all right.

637
00:54:34.100 --> 00:54:35.314
All right. listen to me..

638
00:54:38.105 --> 00:54:39.148
Where are you going?

639
00:54:39.388 --> 00:54:40.861
To our farm.

640
00:54:42.785 --> 00:54:43.828
Open the back.

641
00:54:44.208 --> 00:54:45.775
As you wish. as you wish.

642
00:54:50.672 --> 00:54:52.828
Oh. easy. easy.
Take it easy. chaps.

643
00:55:08.189 --> 00:55:10.907
- Guard: Anything back there?
- Nothing. it's empty.

644
00:55:14.280 --> 00:55:15.923
- Everything okay?
- Yes.

645
00:55:39.204 --> 00:55:40.795
- Where's Shaw?
- I know her.

646
00:55:41.552 --> 00:55:44.678
She's the telepath. and I read her. she'll know we're here.

647
00:55:45.946 --> 00:55:47.945
Let me try something else.

648
00:56:05.615 --> 00:56:08.311
Shaw sends his apologies. but
he's indisposed.

649
00:56:08.312 --> 00:56:09.855
He asked me to come in his place.

650
00:56:10.815 --> 00:56:15.084
But between you and I honey.
I'm a lot better company.

651
00:56:15.897 --> 00:56:17.289
Please come in.

652
00:56:21.865 --> 00:56:23.131
He's not coming.

653
00:56:25.572 --> 00:56:29.340
- So. what now. boss?
- Now. nothing. We're here for Shaw.

654
00:56:29.484 --> 00:56:30.985
- Mission aborted
- The hell it is.

655
00:56:31.138 --> 00:56:33.506
- Erik.
-She's his right hand woman.

656
00:56:33.508 --> 00:56:34.979
That's good enough for me.

657
00:56:34.980 --> 00:56:37.691
The CIA invading the home of a senior
Soviet official.

658
00:56:37.824 --> 00:56:40.388
- Are you crazy?
- I'm not CIA.

659
00:56:41.321 --> 00:56:42.401
Erik!

660
00:56:44.400 --> 00:56:46.674
To your health.

661
00:56:50.774 --> 00:56:52.730
So you must be busy
planning your next move.

662
00:56:52.852 --> 00:56:56.310
What with the American's refusing to remove
their missiles from Turkey.

663
00:56:57.564 --> 00:57:00.922
You know I can't talk about those things. Miss Frost.

664
00:57:01.350 --> 00:57:02.770
Emma.

665
00:57:05.762 --> 00:57:09.763
And don't worry. you don't have to say a word.

666
00:57:26.462 --> 00:57:28.089
He's going to start
world war III single handed.

667
00:57:28.183 --> 00:57:30.108
- We have to do something.
- Like what?

668
00:57:30.527 --> 00:57:32.266
- We're moving out.
- You can't.

669
00:57:47.753 --> 00:57:50.162
I'm sorry. I can't leave him.

670
00:58:02.200 --> 00:58:03.458
For goodness sake. Erik...

671
00:58:04.232 --> 00:58:04.842
Be calm.

672
00:58:05.311 --> 00:58:08.888
Be calm.
Forget my face. Yes.

673
00:58:13.799 --> 00:58:14.842
(Speaking Russian)

674
00:58:17.979 --> 00:58:22.124
You're beautiful. so beautiful...yes.

675
00:58:22.723 --> 00:58:24.180
Pathetic.

676
00:58:31.396 --> 00:58:32.438
You are.

677
00:58:36.164 --> 00:58:37.581
Nice trick.

678
00:58:39.777 --> 00:58:41.176
Who are  you?

679
00:58:45.141 --> 00:58:46.143
Go to sleep.

680
00:58:54.428 --> 00:58:56.883
You can stop trying to read my mind. sugar.

681
00:58:58.814 --> 00:59:01.725
You're never going to get anything
from me while I'm like this.

682
00:59:14.407 --> 00:59:16.149
So then you can just tell us.

683
00:59:18.585 --> 00:59:20.215
Where is Shaw?

684
00:59:26.652 --> 00:59:27.794
Erik.

685
00:59:34.367 --> 00:59:35.601
Erik. that's enough.

686
00:59:44.358 --> 00:59:46.008
Erik. that's enough!

687
00:59:55.636 --> 00:59:56.903
All yours.

688
00:59:58.182 --> 01:00:00.319
She won't be shifting into diamond form again.

689
01:00:01.297 --> 01:00:03.610
But if she does. just give her a gentle tap.

690
01:00:29.730 --> 01:00:32.356
<i>We are the children of the atom.</i>

691
01:00:32.808 --> 01:00:35.419
<i>Radiation gave birth to mutants.</i>

692
01:00:35.805 --> 01:00:39.751
<i>What will kill the humans.
will only make us stronger.</i>

693
01:00:44.475 --> 01:00:45.961
Beautiful. isn't it?

694
01:00:48.982 --> 01:00:51.309
This is worse that we previously imagined.

695
01:00:53.638 --> 01:00:55.298
We're taking you with us.

696
01:00:55.515 --> 01:00:59.131
- CIA will want to question you themselves.
- I doubt it.

697
01:00:59.505 --> 01:01:01.825
Might be other things to worry about right now.

698
01:01:08.095 --> 01:01:09.939
Whoa. all right.

699
01:01:10.390 --> 01:01:14.739
- Jesus. man you are killing me.
- Don't beat yourself up. we got a lot of spare time.

700
01:01:20.335 --> 01:01:22.643
Oh. I didn't know the circus was in town.

701
01:01:22.745 --> 01:01:25.325
CIA Agent: Hey come on honey. give us a little. uh...
(Making fluttering sounds)

702
01:01:25.480 --> 01:01:29.781
No? Come on. let's see the foot.
There it is. come on Bigfoot let's go.

703
01:01:29.909 --> 01:01:31.817
Hey. hey come on. hey.

704
01:01:36.496 --> 01:01:38.352
They're just guys being stupid.

705
01:01:38.621 --> 01:01:41.997
Guy's being stupid I can handle.
Okay. I've handled that my whole life.

706
01:01:42.122 --> 01:01:44.529
But I'd rather have a bunch of guys
stare at me with my clothes off.

707
01:01:44.624 --> 01:01:47.021
then the way these one's stare at me.

708
01:01:47.991 --> 01:01:49.301
At us.

709
01:01:57.315 --> 01:01:58.529
What was that?

710
01:02:00.737 --> 01:02:02.547
I don't know. but
something doesn't feel right.

711
01:02:11.574 --> 01:02:15.907
- Man in Black: No news of Shaw?
- Agent: Not a peep. nothing through that back channel.

712
01:02:29.237 --> 01:02:30.427
What is that?

713
01:02:39.938 --> 01:02:40.981
Ahhhh.

714
01:02:48.178 --> 01:02:49.729
We have an intruder on the main atrium.

715
01:02:49.981 --> 01:02:52.602
- Where are the mutants?
- You take another step. I'm going to put you down.

716
01:02:52.836 --> 01:02:55.358
Of course you will. but where do I find
the more evolved people?

717
01:02:57.142 --> 01:02:58.224
Send back-up now!

718
01:03:01.452 --> 01:03:04.010
Get back. get back. do not leave that room.
We're under attack.

719
01:03:04.322 --> 01:03:06.380
- Look out!
- Shoot it. shoot it!

720
01:03:20.279 --> 01:03:21.300
Where are the mutants?

721
01:03:21.529 --> 01:03:23.556
Put that man down or we will open fire.

722
01:03:49.105 --> 01:03:51.650
Stay here my ass.
Let's go!

723
01:03:56.864 --> 01:03:58.697
- Get back!
- We can help. we can help!

724
01:04:59.840 --> 01:05:02.667
Wait. wait. you want the mutants?
They're right through that door.

725
01:05:02.709 --> 01:05:04.124
Just let us normal people go.

726
01:05:04.405 --> 01:05:05.696
We're no threa...

727
01:05:15.009 --> 01:05:15.951
Where's the telepath?

728
01:05:16.785 --> 01:05:18.492
- Not here.
- To bad.

729
01:05:19.306 --> 01:05:21.029
Now I can take this silly thing off.

730
01:05:23.559 --> 01:05:26.358
Good evening
My name's. Sebastian Shaw.

731
01:05:28.629 --> 01:05:30.895
And I am not here to hurt you.

732
01:05:31.242 --> 01:05:32.036
Freeze!

733
01:05:32.884 --> 01:05:33.750
Azazel...

734
01:05:37.671 --> 01:05:40.366
My friends. there's a revolution coming.

735
01:05:40.846 --> 01:05:44.123
When mankind discovers who we are.
what we can do.

736
01:05:44.411 --> 01:05:46.018
Each of us will face a choice.

737
01:05:46.901 --> 01:05:51.379
Be enslaved. or rise up to rule.

738
01:05:52.404 --> 01:05:54.914
Choose freely. but know that if you are not with us.

739
01:05:54.915 --> 01:05:58.403
then by definition you are against us.

740
01:05:59.258 --> 01:06:05.258
So. you can stay. and fight for the
people who hate. and fear you.

741
01:06:06.154 --> 01:06:10.317
Or you can join me.
And live like kings.

742
01:06:16.531 --> 01:06:17.866
And Queens.

743
01:06:29.662 --> 01:06:31.341
- Angel?
- Are you kidding me?

744
01:06:32.174 --> 01:06:35.334
Come on. we don't belong here.

745
01:06:36.191 --> 01:06:38.166
And that's nothing to be ashamed of.

746
01:06:43.432 --> 01:06:44.781
We have to do something.

747
01:07:00.622 --> 01:07:03.628
Stop. I'm coming with you.

748
01:07:07.446 --> 01:07:08.551
Good choice.

749
01:07:10.204 --> 01:07:12.297
So tell me about your mutation.

750
01:07:13.037 --> 01:07:14.634
Well. I adapt to survive.

751
01:07:18.176 --> 01:07:21.279
- So I guess I'm coming with you.
- I like that.

752
01:07:28.174 --> 01:07:30.371
- Alex................do it!
- Get down!

753
01:07:36.140 --> 01:07:37.582
Protecting your fellow mutants?

754
01:07:39.044 --> 01:07:42.032
It's a noble gesture.
Feels good.

755
01:07:48.394 --> 01:07:49.858
Adapt to this.

756
01:08:20.231 --> 01:08:24.248
Moscow. Russia

757
01:08:33.985 --> 01:08:35.028
Hello.

758
01:08:36.698 --> 01:08:44.987
Once again. my sympathies for your
treatment at the hands of the CIA.

759
01:08:45.604 --> 01:08:47.376
These Americans are ruthless.

760
01:08:48.364 --> 01:08:52.524
Now they have their missiles placed in Turkey.

761
01:08:53.709 --> 01:08:58.440
I expect you'll be planning
missile sites of your own.

762
01:08:58.558 --> 01:09:04.873
Somewhere you know the American
early-warning system won't help.

763
01:09:05.486 --> 01:09:09.746
I hear Cuba is lovely this time of year.

764
01:09:10.164 --> 01:09:12.957
And so close to Florida.

765
01:09:14.038 --> 01:09:15.732
Missiles in Cuba?

766
01:09:18.277 --> 01:09:19.630
You're serious?

767
01:09:20.646 --> 01:09:23.254
We may as well declare war.

768
01:09:24.493 --> 01:09:26.420
Maybe I wasn't clear enough.

769
01:09:28.930 --> 01:09:30.837
You will make this happen.

770
01:09:33.367 --> 01:09:34.400
Okay.

771
01:09:35.097 --> 01:09:37.580
Let's see what KGB think about this.

772
01:09:42.030 --> 01:09:45.160
Hello. General Armivolkoff.

773
01:09:48.401 --> 01:09:50.194
It's nothing.

774
01:10:06.760 --> 01:10:07.522
Raven.

775
01:10:13.875 --> 01:10:15.822
Charles: We've made arrangements for you to
be taken home immediately.

776
01:10:16.104 --> 01:10:17.455
- Sean: We're not going home.
- What?

777
01:10:18.010 --> 01:10:21.395
- He's not going back to prison.
- They killed. Darwin.

778
01:10:21.396 --> 01:10:22.933
Charles: All the more reason for you to leave.

779
01:10:23.160 --> 01:10:24.066
This is over.

780
01:10:24.546 --> 01:10:28.640
Darwin's dead. Charles.
And we can't even bury him.

781
01:10:31.241 --> 01:10:32.759
We can avenge him.

782
01:10:36.244 --> 01:10:37.597
Erik. word please.

783
01:10:41.636 --> 01:10:44.246
- They're just kids.
- No. they were kids.

784
01:10:44.813 --> 01:10:46.958
Shaw has his army. we need ours.

785
01:10:53.060 --> 01:10:56.228
Charles: We'll have to train.
All of us.

786
01:10:57.137 --> 01:10:58.914
- Yes?
- Yeah.

787
01:10:59.816 --> 01:11:01.105
Well we can't stay here.

788
01:11:01.589 --> 01:11:04.013
Even if they reopen the department.
it's not safe.

789
01:11:04.988 --> 01:11:06.987
We've got no where to go.

790
01:11:09.760 --> 01:11:10.950
Yes. we do.

791
01:11:11.587 --> 01:11:13.394
McCone: The law says we've got to turn her over.

792
01:11:13.659 --> 01:11:15.730
Stryker: The law applies to human beings.

793
01:11:15.969 --> 01:11:19.032
The same laws don't apply to mutants.
They're to dangerous.

794
01:11:19.352 --> 01:11:23.009
Times like this. security is more
important than liberty.

795
01:11:23.563 --> 01:11:28.226
- There's a war coming. John.
- McCone: Yes. but a war with who?

796
01:11:42.463 --> 01:11:43.652
Excellent question.

797
01:11:44.683 --> 01:11:46.504
Though I won't call it a war exactly.

798
01:11:47.537 --> 01:11:50.467
That suggests both sides stand an
equal chance of winning.

799
01:12:00.727 --> 01:12:02.678
Captain. no sign of any American Ships.

800
01:12:03.395 --> 01:12:05.825
Maintain course. full ahead.

801
01:12:06.438 --> 01:12:08.930
The Russians have
sent their warheads to Cuba.

802
01:12:09.386 --> 01:12:11.470
We have a week before their ship hits the coast.

803
01:12:11.735 --> 01:12:15.866
Our fleet can be on this line.
when the Russian missile ship arrives.

804
01:12:16.565 --> 01:12:21.532
If that ship crosses the line. they will have
declared war against the United States.

805
01:12:22.567 --> 01:12:25.497
We will have no choice but to retaliate
with a full nuclear response.

806
01:12:26.501 --> 01:12:27.755
Do we agree?

807
01:12:32.894 --> 01:12:34.184
Man: Dispatch the Seventh fleet.

808
01:12:37.570 --> 01:12:41.104
- This is yours?
- No. it's ours.

809
01:12:47.588 --> 01:12:50.407
Honestly Charles. I don't know how you survived.

810
01:12:50.925 --> 01:12:52.462
Living in such hardship.

811
01:12:52.765 --> 01:12:55.345
Well it was a hardship softened by me.

812
01:12:58.657 --> 01:13:01.189
Come on. time for the tour.

813
01:13:08.384 --> 01:13:12.254
Moscow. Russia

814
01:13:14.230 --> 01:13:15.950
Dear comrades.

815
01:13:15.951 --> 01:13:23.517
The United States have dispatched
war ships for Cuba.

816
01:13:24.099 --> 01:13:28.019
This leaves us with no choice.

817
01:13:29.359 --> 01:13:32.778
Comrade First Secretary.

818
01:13:33.523 --> 01:13:36.622
We must send in our fleet.

819
01:13:39.360 --> 01:13:41.326
Dispatch the fleet!

820
01:13:46.223 --> 01:13:49.062
<i>President Kennedy has
signed a formal proclamation.</i>

821
01:13:49.265 --> 01:13:52.948
<i>Setting up a blockade of all missiles.
armed for Cuba.</i>

822
01:13:54.027 --> 01:14:00.261
<i>The Soviet Union reacted by terming it
as step along the road to unleashing a thermal nuclear war.</i>

823
01:14:10.943 --> 01:14:13.341
- You're sure?
- I'm sure.

824
01:14:14.369 --> 01:14:15.097
All right.

825
01:14:22.456 --> 01:14:24.526
No. no I can't I'm sorry.

826
01:14:24.770 --> 01:14:25.925
I can't shoot anybody point blank.

827
01:14:26.155 --> 01:14:26.909
let alone my friend.

828
01:14:27.186 --> 01:14:28.815
Oh come on. you know I can deflect it.

829
01:14:29.059 --> 01:14:30.313
You're always telling me I should push myself.

830
01:14:30.634 --> 01:14:33.779
If you know you can deflect it. then
you're not challenging yourself.

831
01:14:35.511 --> 01:14:38.137
What ever happened to the man
who was trying to raise a submarine?

832
01:14:39.208 --> 01:14:39.961
What. I can't.

833
01:14:41.155 --> 01:14:43.620
Something that big. I need the situation. the anger.

834
01:14:43.850 --> 01:14:45.227
No. the anger's not enough.

835
01:14:46.161 --> 01:14:47.758
Well it's gotten the job done all this time.

836
01:14:48.018 --> 01:14:49.573
It's nearly gotten you killed all this time.

837
01:14:51.112 --> 01:14:51.942
Hey. come here.

838
01:14:53.095 --> 01:14:55.120
Let's try something a little more challenging.

839
01:14:56.451 --> 01:14:59.483
My step-father took the possibility
of nuclear war quite seriously.

840
01:14:59.732 --> 01:15:00.670
This way.

841
01:15:00.809 --> 01:15:02.932
That's why he had this bunker built down here.

842
01:15:03.180 --> 01:15:05.507
I thought we could use it as a practice range of sort.

843
01:15:05.728 --> 01:15:07.180
You don't think I'm going to blow though the walls?

844
01:15:07.486 --> 01:15:09.992
No. he had this place built to
with stand a nuclear bomb.

845
01:15:10.216 --> 01:15:11.670
I think it can handle you. Alex.

846
01:15:11.936 --> 01:15:14.047
You know when I do this.
bad things tend to happen.

847
01:15:15.069 --> 01:15:18.534
That's because you can't control it.
It controls you.

848
01:15:19.093 --> 01:15:21.780
That's why we're here. Alex.
It's part of your training.

849
01:15:26.869 --> 01:15:28.088
What you're doing is incredible.

850
01:15:28.357 --> 01:15:31.046
You're hitting a pitch with sound waves at
the same resonate frequency of the glass.

851
01:15:31.047 --> 01:15:32.147
That's why it shatters.

852
01:15:32.148 --> 01:15:34.757
But this. it's like any
other muscle in the body.

853
01:15:34.758 --> 01:15:35.810
You can control it.

854
01:15:37.736 --> 01:15:40.210
<i>"In each of us. two natures are at war."</i>

855
01:15:40.698 --> 01:15:42.122
Robert Louis Stevenson.
"Jekyll and Hyde".

856
01:15:42.425 --> 01:15:43.170
Top marks.

857
01:15:43.673 --> 01:15:45.538
Still it really wasn't really about good
and evil. Was it. Hank.

858
01:15:45.742 --> 01:15:48.764
It was about man's animal nature.
and his struggle to control it.

859
01:15:48.969 --> 01:15:49.940
To conform.

860
01:15:50.207 --> 01:15:52.243
It is that struggle which is holding you back.

861
01:15:52.918 --> 01:15:55.167
Jekyll is afraid of what he could be capable of.

862
01:15:55.605 --> 01:15:56.593
You are too.

863
01:15:57.210 --> 01:15:59.496
If you're serious about me doing this.
you might want to get back.

864
01:15:59.940 --> 01:16:03.955
- Of course. should I shut the door?
- Yeah.

865
01:16:06.616 --> 01:16:07.492
Whenever you're ready.

866
01:16:14.272 --> 01:16:16.341
Oh my god.

867
01:16:20.125 --> 01:16:22.112
Charles: I will teach you to control this. Alex.

868
01:16:25.471 --> 01:16:26.926
Sean: You're sure that this will work.

869
01:16:27.638 --> 01:16:29.744
Anything is possible. I based the design...

870
01:16:29.746 --> 01:16:32.078
Hank. stop talking.
Come on.

871
01:16:32.222 --> 01:16:33.961
Now remember. scream as hard as you can.

872
01:16:34.232 --> 01:16:35.889
You need the sound waves to be supersonic.

873
01:16:36.107 --> 01:16:37.852
Catch them at the right angle.
and they should carry you.

874
01:16:38.609 --> 01:16:41.754
"They should carry me."
That's reassuring.

875
01:16:42.652 --> 01:16:43.506
Good luck.

876
01:16:44.262 --> 01:16:45.537
And don't forget to scream.

877
01:16:52.502 --> 01:16:53.544
Ahh.

878
01:16:55.502 --> 01:16:58.720
If you want to beat me this time.
you have to set the beast free.

879
01:17:00.389 --> 01:17:04.090
On your marks. get set...GO!

880
01:17:19.613 --> 01:17:20.808
Oh. congratulations my friend.

881
01:17:21.496 --> 01:17:23.055
Robert Louis Stevenson
would have been proud.

882
01:17:25.295 --> 01:17:26.219
Impressive. Hank.

883
01:17:26.888 --> 01:17:28.663
Feet like those. all you need is a red nose.

884
01:17:29.051 --> 01:17:29.974
Right. Bozo?

885
01:17:30.837 --> 01:17:32.294
- I'm done here.
- Thank you. Alex

886
01:17:34.010 --> 01:17:34.941
Come on. Hank.

887
01:17:46.130 --> 01:17:48.981
 If you're using half the
concentration to look normal.

888
01:17:49.362 --> 01:17:51.998
Then you're only half paying attention to
whatever else you do.

889
01:17:52.270 --> 01:17:55.095
Just pointing out something that could save your life.

890
01:17:59.754 --> 01:18:01.528
You want society to accept you.

891
01:18:02.514 --> 01:18:04.287
But you can't even accept yourself.

892
01:18:11.046 --> 01:18:11.946
Sexy.

893
01:18:13.223 --> 01:18:14.052
This is just the prototype.

894
01:18:14.254 --> 01:18:16.447
The real one will look considerably better.
it'll be a whole suit.

895
01:18:16.748 --> 01:18:21.737
See these sensors measure your energy output.
this panel focuses it and the excess is absorbed.

896
01:18:21.841 --> 01:18:24.141
All right try hitting the one in the middle.
just the one in the middle. mind.

897
01:18:25.081 --> 01:18:25.804
Charles: Good luck.

898
01:18:32.649 --> 01:18:33.692
Oomph!

899
01:18:36.296 --> 01:18:39.015
You ought to see this. Your genes are
extraordinary. you know that.

900
01:18:39.142 --> 01:18:40.979
Your cells age at half the rate of a normal human.

901
01:18:41.210 --> 01:18:43.174
When you're forty you will still
have the looks of a teenager.

902
01:18:43.877 --> 01:18:47.169
You have the most incredible cellular
structure I've ever seen.

903
01:18:52.671 --> 01:18:54.398
You truly believe I'll fly this time?

904
01:18:54.659 --> 01:18:55.935
Charles: Unreservedly.

905
01:18:56.353 --> 01:18:57.573
- I trust you.
- I'm touched.

906
01:18:57.808 --> 01:18:59.172
- I don't trust him.
- Say nothing.

907
01:19:00.737 --> 01:19:01.582
I'm going to die!

908
01:19:02.003 --> 01:19:04.398
All right. look we're not going to make you do anything
that your not so...

909
01:19:04.399 --> 01:19:05.636
Here. let me help him.

910
01:19:07.579 --> 01:19:08.622
Erik!

911
01:19:20.158 --> 01:19:22.864
Whaoooo!

912
01:19:27.716 --> 01:19:29.261
Wahhh hooo!

913
01:19:29.888 --> 01:19:30.895
What?

914
01:19:31.079 --> 01:19:32.865
You know you were thinking the same.

915
01:19:34.035 --> 01:19:37.402
Wonderful work Hank. thank you very much.
All right Alex. I want you to hit the X.

916
01:19:38.172 --> 01:19:39.943
And try not to hit me. there's a good chap.

917
01:19:40.755 --> 01:19:43.406
- You're serious?
- I'm very serious.

918
01:19:43.820 --> 01:19:45.773
I have complete and utter faith in you.

919
01:19:58.638 --> 01:20:02.363
- Am I still a Bozo?
- Yes. Hank. You're still a Bozo.

920
01:20:03.607 --> 01:20:04.849
But nice job.

921
01:20:07.926 --> 01:20:08.866
See that?

922
01:20:09.691 --> 01:20:11.135
Try turning it to face us.

923
01:20:30.813 --> 01:20:36.192
You know. I believe the true focus lies
somewhere between rage and serenity.

924
01:20:37.890 --> 01:20:40.059
Would you mind. if I...?

925
01:21:14.159 --> 01:21:15.467
What did you just do to me?

926
01:21:16.833 --> 01:21:20.397
I accessed the brightest corner
of your memory system.

927
01:21:22.358 --> 01:21:24.748
It's a very beautiful memory Erik. thank you.

928
01:21:25.854 --> 01:21:27.721
I didn't know I still had that.

929
01:21:28.986 --> 01:21:31.041
There's so much more to you than you know.

930
01:21:31.727 --> 01:21:36.806
Not just pain. and anger.
There's good too. I felt it.

931
01:21:37.814 --> 01:21:39.896
And when you can access all that.

932
01:21:40.241 --> 01:21:42.875
You will possess a power no one can match.

933
01:21:44.128 --> 01:21:45.477
Not even me.

934
01:21:47.340 --> 01:21:49.496
So. come on. Try again.

935
01:22:30.494 --> 01:22:31.223
- Hey!
-Well done.

936
01:22:31.791 --> 01:22:33.605
The President is about to make his address.

937
01:22:35.770 --> 01:22:39.861
<i>TV announcer: It shall be the policy of this nation
to regard any nuclear missile.</i>

938
01:22:40.022 --> 01:22:43.307
<i>...crossing the embargo line. that surrounds Cuba.</i>

939
01:22:43.612 --> 01:22:47.372
<i>As an attack by the Soviet Union
on the United States.</i>

940
01:22:47.871 --> 01:22:51.914
<i>Requiring a full retaliatory response.
Upon the Soviet Union.</i>

941
01:22:51.915 --> 01:22:54.004
- That’s' where we're going to find. Shaw'
- How do you know?

942
01:22:54.258 --> 01:22:57.794
Two super powers facing off. and
he want's to start world war III.

943
01:22:58.700 --> 01:23:00.140
He won't leave anything to chance.

944
01:23:00.567 --> 01:23:04.283
So much for diplomacy.
I suggest you all get a good nights sleep.

945
01:23:04.287 --> 01:23:07.075
<i>...ultimately leads to war.</i>

946
01:23:07.610 --> 01:23:11.488
<i>TV announcer: Tensions mount as the Soviet Missile
ship nears Cuba.</i>

947
01:23:12.062 --> 01:23:16.383
<i>All diplomatic efforts to avert
Nuclear war have thus far failed.</i>

948
01:23:16.917 --> 01:23:21.166
<i>As the American people ready themselves.
for the likelihood of an atomic attack.</i>

949
01:23:21.431 --> 01:23:23.900
<i>There are widespread reports of panic buying.</i>

950
01:23:24.698 --> 01:23:26.278
<i>Supermarkets cleared.</i>

951
01:23:26.516 --> 01:23:29.170
<i>As shelters unused since the second world war.</i>

952
01:23:29.418 --> 01:23:31.594
<i>are stocked for what may lie ahead.</i>

953
01:23:32.003 --> 01:23:36.118
<i>In all its history. America has never
faced a greater threat.</i>

954
01:23:36.671 --> 01:23:40.356
The world is primed for war.
And there's no one to stop me.

955
01:23:45.148 --> 01:23:47.009
Come in.

956
01:23:47.879 --> 01:23:48.881
Hey.

957
01:23:50.228 --> 01:23:51.230
Got a surprise for you.

958
01:24:00.661 --> 01:24:03.596
I isolated the right marker in your DNA sample.

959
01:24:04.287 --> 01:24:05.992
The serum works like an anti-biotic.

960
01:24:06.291 --> 01:24:08.849
Attacking the cells that cause our physical mutation.

961
01:24:09.504 --> 01:24:11.507
It won't affect our abilities.
just our appearance.

962
01:24:15.000 --> 01:24:16.511
Do you still want to do this?

963
01:24:17.896 --> 01:24:19.743
Should we have to hide?

964
01:24:21.310 --> 01:24:22.313
You already do.

965
01:24:23.291 --> 01:24:25.790
You're hiding right now.
Like I have my whole life.

966
01:24:26.952 --> 01:24:29.471
I don't want to feel like a freak. all the time.

967
01:24:29.472 --> 01:24:31.219
- I just want to look...
- ...normal.

968
01:24:31.627 --> 01:24:32.507
Yeah.

969
01:24:39.872 --> 01:24:41.314
Hank. don't.

970
01:24:43.215 --> 01:24:47.331
You're beautiful. Hank.
Everything you are. you're perfect.

971
01:24:50.151 --> 01:24:53.184
Raven: Look at all of us. Look at
all we've achieved this week.

972
01:24:53.538 --> 01:24:55.187
All we will achieve.

973
01:24:56.755 --> 01:25:01.689
We are different. But we shouldn't
be trying to fit into society.

974
01:25:02.839 --> 01:25:05.228
Society should aspire and be more like us.

975
01:25:06.922 --> 01:25:09.920
Mutant. and proud.

976
01:25:15.137 --> 01:25:18.871
It behooves me to tell you.
but even if we save the world tomorrow.

977
01:25:19.075 --> 01:25:21.239
And mutants are accepted into society.

978
01:25:22.189 --> 01:25:24.906
My feet and your natural blue form.

979
01:25:25.965 --> 01:25:27.721
Will never be deemed beautiful.

980
01:25:33.379 --> 01:25:34.763
You look beautiful now.

981
01:25:36.757 --> 01:25:39.765
We need this cure.

982
01:26:06.796 --> 01:26:11.762
Cuba. Russia. America makes no difference.

983
01:26:12.716 --> 01:26:15.352
Shaw's declared war on mankind.
on all of us.

984
01:26:15.844 --> 01:26:21.817
- He has to be stopped.
- I'm not going to stop Shaw. I'm going to kill him.

985
01:26:25.097 --> 01:26:26.862
Do you have it in you to allow that?

986
01:26:33.415 --> 01:26:35.702
You've known all along
why I was here. Charles.

987
01:26:36.172 --> 01:26:37.441
But things have changed.

988
01:26:38.493 --> 01:26:40.547
What started as a covert mission.

989
01:26:40.785 --> 01:26:43.789
...tomorrow mankind will know that mutants exist.

990
01:26:43.792 --> 01:26:46.017
Shaw. us... they won't differentiate.

991
01:26:46.633 --> 01:26:50.090
They'll fear us. and that
fear will turn to hatred.

992
01:26:50.548 --> 01:26:53.727
Not if we stop a war.
Not if we can prevent. Shaw.

993
01:26:53.962 --> 01:26:55.765
Not if we risk our lives doing so.

994
01:26:56.047 --> 01:26:57.097
Would they do the same for us?

995
01:26:57.379 --> 01:26:58.869
We have it in us to be the better men.

996
01:26:59.119 --> 01:27:00.659
We already are.

997
01:27:01.093 --> 01:27:02.662
We're the next stage of human evolution.

998
01:27:02.882 --> 01:27:04.386
- You said it yourself.
- Enough.

999
01:27:04.985 --> 01:27:06.853
Are you really so naive?

1000
01:27:06.854 --> 01:27:09.530
As to think they won't battle their own extinction?

1001
01:27:11.084 --> 01:27:13.400
- Or is it arrogance?
- I'm sorry.

1002
01:27:14.652 --> 01:27:16.493
After tomorrow they're going to turn on us.

1003
01:27:16.644 --> 01:27:19.883
And you're blind to it. because you
believe they're all like Moira.

1004
01:27:20.185 --> 01:27:22.002
And you believe they're all like. Shaw.

1005
01:27:24.516 --> 01:27:27.364
Listen to me. very carefully my friend.

1006
01:27:28.651 --> 01:27:31.693
Killing Shaw will not bring you peace.

1007
01:27:33.386 --> 01:27:35.321
Peace was never an option.

1008
01:28:21.004 --> 01:28:23.903
No.

1009
01:28:25.618 --> 01:28:26.660
No.

1010
01:28:55.375 --> 01:28:56.409
Well...

1011
01:28:58.822 --> 01:29:00.143
This is a surprise.

1012
01:29:00.645 --> 01:29:01.838
The nice kind?

1013
01:29:03.917 --> 01:29:06.303
Get out. Raven. I want to go to bed.

1014
01:29:07.545 --> 01:29:08.884
Maybe in a few years.

1015
01:29:13.874 --> 01:29:14.987
How about now?

1016
01:29:20.587 --> 01:29:22.134
I prefer the real. Raven.

1017
01:29:26.035 --> 01:29:28.559
I said the real. Raven.

1018
01:29:38.590 --> 01:29:40.001
Perfection.

1019
01:29:44.348 --> 01:29:47.671
- Could you pass me my robe?
- You don't have to hide.

1020
01:29:52.681 --> 01:29:56.065
Have you ever looked at a tiger.
and thought you'd want to cover it up?

1021
01:29:58.590 --> 01:30:00.238
No. but...

1022
01:30:00.523 --> 01:30:02.225
You're an exquisite creature. Raven.

1023
01:30:04.176 --> 01:30:06.420
All your life the world has tried to tame you.

1024
01:30:07.547 --> 01:30:08.910
It's time for you to be free.

1025
01:30:29.545 --> 01:30:31.545
Raven: You know sometimes I wonder
what my life would have been like.

1026
01:30:31.545 --> 01:30:33.519
If you hadn't found me here that night.

1027
01:30:34.105 --> 01:30:36.343
Fairable. E..gah...ah.

1028
01:30:37.792 --> 01:30:39.127
For gods sake. Raven!

1029
01:30:39.721 --> 01:30:42.071
Where are you clothes?
Pu...put some. put some clothes on.

1030
01:30:42.246 --> 01:30:44.020
That's not what you said when you first saw me.

1031
01:30:44.751 --> 01:30:47.317
But I guess pets are always cuter
when they're little. right?

1032
01:30:48.448 --> 01:30:49.979
Raven. I don't know what's got into you lately.

1033
01:30:50.707 --> 01:30:51.851
I thought you'd be in a good mood.

1034
01:30:52.740 --> 01:30:57.598
Hank tells me that he's found the
answer to your cosmetic problem.

1035
01:30:59.917 --> 01:31:02.328
You going to tell me what's the matter?
Or will I have to read your mind?

1036
01:31:02.558 --> 01:31:04.181
You promised me you would never do that.

1037
01:31:04.488 --> 01:31:08.898
Until recently. I never had to use my powers
to know what you were thinking. Raven.

1038
01:31:09.051 --> 01:31:12.726
You know Charles. I used to think
it was gonna be you and me against the world.

1039
01:31:13.038 --> 01:31:16.587
But no matter how bad the world gets.
you don't want to be against it. do you?

1040
01:31:16.614 --> 01:31:17.710
You want to be a part of it.

1041
01:31:39.976 --> 01:31:41.127
What the hell happened here?

1042
01:31:49.781 --> 01:31:51.048
Hank has been busy.

1043
01:31:51.590 --> 01:31:52.971
Do we really have to wear these?

1044
01:31:53.868 --> 01:31:56.528
As none of us has mutated to endure extreme G force.

1045
01:31:56.747 --> 01:31:59.700
or being riddled by bullets. I suggest we suit up.

1046
01:32:24.631 --> 01:32:25.699
Where's Hank?

1047
01:32:27.858 --> 01:32:29.049
I'm here.

1048
01:32:38.924 --> 01:32:39.801
Hank?

1049
01:32:45.788 --> 01:32:50.173
It didn't attack the cells.
It enhanced them.

1050
01:32:52.696 --> 01:32:53.805
It didn't work.

1051
01:32:54.484 --> 01:32:56.043
Yes it did. Hank.

1052
01:32:56.394 --> 01:33:00.187
Don't you see?
This is who you were meant to be.

1053
01:33:01.317 --> 01:33:02.876
This is you.

1054
01:33:04.701 --> 01:33:06.050
No more hiding.

1055
01:33:06.926 --> 01:33:07.984
Never looked better. man.

1056
01:33:08.534 --> 01:33:09.577
Hank!

1057
01:33:09.578 --> 01:33:10.906
Growls.

1058
01:33:11.158 --> 01:33:13.431
Don't mock me.

1059
01:33:13.793 --> 01:33:15.374
Hank. put him down immediately. please.

1060
01:33:15.515 --> 01:33:16.896
Hank...HANK!

1061
01:33:19.661 --> 01:33:21.222
I wasn't.

1062
01:33:21.519 --> 01:33:23.572
Even I got to admit. you look pretty bad ass.

1063
01:33:23.791 --> 01:33:27.021
I think I got a new name for you. Beast.

1064
01:33:29.363 --> 01:33:33.728
- You sure you can fly this thing?
- Of course I can. I designed it.

1065
01:33:36.261 --> 01:33:40.102
Cuba

1066
01:33:45.981 --> 01:33:47.239
Status of the cargo ship?

1067
01:33:47.890 --> 01:33:51.009
Lieutenant Commander: Bearing 1-8-0. 12 knots.

1068
01:33:53.240 --> 01:33:55.498
Three minutes to the embargo line. sir.

1069
01:33:56.699 --> 01:33:58.710
God help them if they cross it.

1070
01:34:01.107 --> 01:34:02.643
God help us all.

1071
01:34:03.114 --> 01:34:06.379
- Lieutenant Commander: Sound general quarters.
- Officers: General quarters. general quarters.

1072
01:34:06.659 --> 01:34:09.121
- All hands man battle stations!
- Yes sir.

1073
01:34:09.417 --> 01:34:11.214
Set conditions. zero.

1074
01:34:11.904 --> 01:34:14.081
General quarters. battle stations.

1075
01:34:23.469 --> 01:34:28.798
Captain. we already have our orders.
Why so eager for new ones?

1076
01:34:29.826 --> 01:34:33.515
I lived through one war. Comrade.

1077
01:34:34.669 --> 01:34:36.758
I'd prefer not to start another.

1078
01:34:39.216 --> 01:34:41.248
Battle stations.
Now!

1079
01:34:44.299 --> 01:34:49.051
Gun boss. target
cargo ship. bearing 1-8-zero.

1080
01:34:51.136 --> 01:34:54.157
Fleet reports all weapons ready.

1081
01:34:54.344 --> 01:34:56.265
Communications officer: From the Kremlin. sir.

1082
01:34:56.684 --> 01:35:00.714
New orders. As of 1025 hours. the cargo
vessel Aral sea. is hereby ordered to...

1083
01:35:00.716 --> 01:35:04.004
...reverse course and return to port in Odessa.

1084
01:35:04.005 --> 01:35:05.467
Aral Sea. come in.

1085
01:35:06.177 --> 01:35:07.855
Aral Sea. come in.

1086
01:35:08.848 --> 01:35:10.264
They are not responding.

1087
01:35:10.265 --> 01:35:11.841
Officer: She's not turning around.

1088
01:35:11.842 --> 01:35:14.477
Aral Sea. you are ordered to turn around.

1089
01:35:14.478 --> 01:35:16.195
Do not cross the line.

1090
01:35:17.153 --> 01:35:19.019
Target ready to be fired upon. sir.

1091
01:35:19.085 --> 01:35:21.852
- Stand by to fire.
- Standing by. sir.

1092
01:35:34.519 --> 01:35:36.273
Looks pretty messy out there.

1093
01:35:47.114 --> 01:35:50.111
Aral Sea.
you are ordered to turn around.

1094
01:35:50.946 --> 01:35:53.708
The crew of the Aral Sea are all dead.
Shaw's been there.

1095
01:35:53.709 --> 01:35:55.484
He's still here. somewhere.

1096
01:35:55.485 --> 01:35:57.041
He's set the ship on course for the embargo line.

1097
01:35:57.260 --> 01:35:59.585
That ship crosses the line. our
boys are going to blow it up.

1098
01:36:00.002 --> 01:36:01.409
Moria: And the war begins.

1099
01:36:02.055 --> 01:36:04.147
Unless they're not on board.

1100
01:36:06.671 --> 01:36:08.827
<i>USS Independence.
this is. Alexander Nevski.</i>

1101
01:36:09.242 --> 01:36:11.477
We have lost control of our cargo ship.

1102
01:36:11.478 --> 01:36:14.274
She's been instructed to stop.
Do not fire.

1103
01:36:14.275 --> 01:36:16.104
Repeat. do not fire.

1104
01:36:16.114 --> 01:36:17.932
They've signaled their
cargo ship to turn around. sir.

1105
01:36:19.428 --> 01:36:23.329
It's a ruse. pay no attention.
Stand by to fire.

1106
01:36:23.516 --> 01:36:25.711
- Standing by to fire. sir.
- On my count.

1107
01:36:26.262 --> 01:36:28.047
Five...four...

1108
01:36:51.176 --> 01:36:53.492
Hold on! Hold on!

1109
01:37:02.320 --> 01:37:03.147
No!

1110
01:37:07.858 --> 01:37:11.504
- What was that?
- The Russians. they have fired on their own ship.

1111
01:37:12.057 --> 01:37:14.083
A little warning next time. professor.

1112
01:37:14.177 --> 01:37:14.977
Sorry about that.

1113
01:37:15.196 --> 01:37:16.777
- You all right?
- Yeah.

1114
01:37:17.551 --> 01:37:19.319
 Son of a...

1115
01:37:19.320 --> 01:37:21.639
Give me Sin-clan on the horn. I want a new set of orders.

1116
01:37:25.410 --> 01:37:27.227
Congratulations. Commander.

1117
01:37:27.837 --> 01:37:31.725
You just averted a nuclear war.

1118
01:37:32.223 --> 01:37:33.266
What?

1119
01:37:33.670 --> 01:37:35.083
Take him to the brig.

1120
01:37:35.335 --> 01:37:37.190
What? What just happened?

1121
01:37:39.013 --> 01:37:40.769
They say the comrade lost his mind.

1122
01:37:41.119 --> 01:37:42.461
The Americans' are applauding.

1123
01:37:44.832 --> 01:37:45.721
They're here.

1124
01:37:45.993 --> 01:37:47.789
That telepath is powerful.

1125
01:37:50.443 --> 01:37:51.990
We're moving to a back-up plan.

1126
01:37:55.389 --> 01:37:57.661
- That was inspired. Charles.
- Thank you very much.

1127
01:37:57.865 --> 01:37:59.100
But I still can't locate Shaw.

1128
01:37:59.352 --> 01:38:01.322
He's down there. we need to find him now.

1129
01:38:01.548 --> 01:38:02.421
Hank?

1130
01:38:02.441 --> 01:38:06.757
- Is there anything unusual on the radar or scanners?
- No. nothing.

1131
01:38:07.472 --> 01:38:11.059
Well then he must be under water.
And obviously we don't have Sonar.

1132
01:38:12.721 --> 01:38:13.538
Yes we do.

1133
01:38:14.603 --> 01:38:15.510
Yes we do.

1134
01:38:20.180 --> 01:38:21.404
Shaw: They were ready for war.

1135
01:38:21.653 --> 01:38:24.211
We just need to strike another match
to light the fuse.

1136
01:38:24.468 --> 01:38:27.233
And we still have the most powerful weapon of all.

1137
01:38:27.978 --> 01:38:28.958
Me.

1138
01:38:29.404 --> 01:38:34.747
Turn the nuclear reactor to 100% output
and make sure I'm not disturbed.

1139
01:38:37.872 --> 01:38:39.983
Hank. level the bloody plane!

1140
01:38:45.426 --> 01:38:47.507
Whoa. you back right off.

1141
01:38:48.445 --> 01:38:50.392
Beast. open the Bombay doors.

1142
01:38:58.649 --> 01:39:02.961
Remember. this is a muscle.
You control it.

1143
01:39:03.242 --> 01:39:07.289
You'll be in here the entire time.
We'll see you soon.

1144
01:39:07.624 --> 01:39:13.785
- On my mark. 3. 2. 1 GO!
- WHOA!!!

1145
01:39:29.745 --> 01:39:32.580
Alert the fleet. they may want to take their cams off.

1146
01:39:45.240 --> 01:39:46.994
Banshee's got a location on Shaw.

1147
01:39:49.755 --> 01:39:50.669
You ready for this?

1148
01:39:51.404 --> 01:39:52.573
Let's find out.

1149
01:40:56.563 --> 01:41:00.887
<i>**Remember. the point between rage and serenity.**</i>

1150
01:42:24.656 --> 01:42:26.260
Erik. take my hand!

1151
01:42:27.117 --> 01:42:30.666
Oh. hold on guys. it's going to get bumpy.

1152
01:42:46.063 --> 01:42:47.964
Erik. take my hand!

1153
01:43:21.617 --> 01:43:22.946
Down.

1154
01:43:38.373 --> 01:43:41.283
- Moira. Moira. are you all right?
- Yeah. I'm okay.

1155
01:43:46.159 --> 01:43:47.834
I read the teleporter's mind.

1156
01:43:48.070 --> 01:43:49.968
Shaw's drawing all of the power out of his sub.

1157
01:43:50.231 --> 01:43:52.208
He's turning himself into some kind of nuclear bomb.

1158
01:43:52.397 --> 01:43:54.457
We've got no time. the Geiger
counter's going out of control.

1159
01:43:54.653 --> 01:43:55.678
All right Moira. this is what we're going to do.

1160
01:43:55.936 --> 01:43:58.115
Get on the radio and tell them to
clear both fleet's out immediately.

1161
01:43:58.360 --> 01:43:59.109
I'm going in.

1162
01:43:59.367 --> 01:44:01.278
Beast. Havok. back him up.

1163
01:44:01.280 --> 01:44:03.148
Erik. I can guide you through once you're in.

1164
01:44:03.379 --> 01:44:05.730
Charles: But I need you to shut down
whatever it is that's blocking me.

1165
01:44:06.011 --> 01:44:07.862
Then we just hope to god it's
not to late for me to stop him.

1166
01:44:07.863 --> 01:44:09.085
- Got it.
- Good luck!

1167
01:44:09.869 --> 01:44:11.760
- Charles: Raven. stop!
- I'm going to help them.

1168
01:44:11.989 --> 01:44:12.767
We don't have time for this.

1169
01:44:13.047 --> 01:44:15.318
Anything comes in that entrance.
you're taking care of it. yes?

1170
01:44:16.246 --> 01:44:16.964
Fine.

1171
01:44:33.222 --> 01:44:34.258
Beeeeaast!

1172
01:44:38.049 --> 01:44:39.898
If we go. you go

1173
01:44:43.119 --> 01:44:45.388
We believe Shaw is trying to
detonate some kind of bomb.

1174
01:44:50.651 --> 01:44:52.647
Erik. make for the middle of the vessel.

1175
01:44:53.127 --> 01:44:54.788
That's the point my mind can't penetrate.

1176
01:44:54.789 --> 01:44:57.002
We have to assume that. that's where Shaw is.

1177
01:45:06.108 --> 01:45:07.677
Gang way. gang way.

1178
01:45:15.032 --> 01:45:17.954
That's the nuclear reactor.
Disable it.

1179
01:45:30.108 --> 01:45:31.876
Navy officer: Stop. don't move.

1180
01:45:39.765 --> 01:45:40.852
Get down!

1181
01:46:04.923 --> 01:46:06.459
<i>**Erik you're there. you've reached the void.**</i>

1182
01:46:06.566 --> 01:46:08.426
He's not here Charles.
Shaw is not here.

1183
01:46:08.509 --> 01:46:10.707
- He's left the sub.
- What? He's got to be there.

1184
01:46:10.929 --> 01:46:13.251
He has to be. there's no where
else he can be. keep looking.

1185
01:46:13.276 --> 01:46:15.853
And I'm telling you he's not.
there's no one here. god damn it!

1186
01:46:19.566 --> 01:46:23.356
Shaw: Erik. what a pleasant surprise.

1187
01:46:23.357 --> 01:46:25.105
Erik?
Erik!

1188
01:46:27.481 --> 01:46:28.859
So good to see you again.

1189
01:46:45.836 --> 01:46:47.449
May I ask you something?

1190
01:46:49.065 --> 01:46:50.586
Why are you on their side?

1191
01:46:51.091 --> 01:46:51.917
- He's gone.
- What?

1192
01:46:52.144 --> 01:46:55.085
He's gone into the void. I can't
communicate with him there.

1193
01:46:55.379 --> 01:46:58.028
Why fight for a doomed race
who will hunt us down.

1194
01:46:58.029 --> 01:47:00.773
...as soon as they realize
their reign is coming to an end.

1195
01:47:29.537 --> 01:47:30.875
Yeah!

1196
01:47:44.651 --> 01:47:46.739
I'm sorry for what happened in the camps.

1197
01:47:48.853 --> 01:47:50.306
I truly am.

1198
01:47:58.811 --> 01:47:59.803
He's back.

1199
01:48:00.188 --> 01:48:03.342
<i>**Erik. whatever you're doing keep
doing it. it's starting to work.**</i>

1200
01:48:04.421 --> 01:48:07.679
But everything I did.
I did for you.

1201
01:48:07.783 --> 01:48:12.060
To unlock your power. To make
you...embrace it.

1202
01:48:15.228 --> 01:48:16.453
<i>**It's working.**</i>

1203
01:48:16.454 --> 01:48:18.852
I'm starting to see him. but I
can't yet touch his mind.

1204
01:48:33.154 --> 01:48:35.733
You've come a long way from bending gates.

1205
01:48:36.267 --> 01:48:37.563
I'm so proud of you.

1206
01:48:45.844 --> 01:48:48.494
And you're just starting to scratch the surface.

1207
01:48:48.720 --> 01:48:53.053
Think how much further we could go. together.

1208
01:49:07.156 --> 01:49:08.199
Roars

1209
01:49:12.949 --> 01:49:15.202
Stop. Azazel!

1210
01:49:30.189 --> 01:49:33.045
I don't want to hurt you. Erik.
I never did.

1211
01:49:33.628 --> 01:49:34.813
I want to help you.

1212
01:49:35.048 --> 01:49:38.398
This is our time.
Our age.

1213
01:49:39.344 --> 01:49:42.656
We are the future of the human race.

1214
01:49:43.750 --> 01:49:48.119
You and me. son.
This world could be ours.

1215
01:49:50.441 --> 01:49:53.544
Everything you did. made me stronger.

1216
01:49:55.329 --> 01:49:57.306
Made me the weapon I am today.

1217
01:49:59.577 --> 01:50:00.787
That's the truth.

1218
01:50:02.437 --> 01:50:04.029
I've known it all along.

1219
01:50:10.549 --> 01:50:12.056
You are my creator.

1220
01:50:12.722 --> 01:50:14.434
- NOW. Charles!
- AHHH!

1221
01:50:15.920 --> 01:50:16.654
Are you okay?

1222
01:50:16.890 --> 01:50:19.629
Moira be quiet. I can only
control this man for so long.

1223
01:50:33.153 --> 01:50:34.412
Sorry. Charles.

1224
01:50:34.413 --> 01:50:36.938
<i>**Erik please. be the better man.
You have it in...**</i>

1225
01:50:36.939 --> 01:50:38.031
But I don’t trust you.

1226
01:50:38.032 --> 01:50:39.534
<i>** Erik. there will be no telling what...**</i>

1227
01:50:41.214 --> 01:50:42.217
No.

1228
01:50:43.153 --> 01:50:45.081
- Charles?
- Don't do this. Erik!

1229
01:50:52.296 --> 01:50:56.756
If you're in there. I'd like you to know
that I agree with every word you've said.

1230
01:50:59.417 --> 01:51:01.208
We are the future.

1231
01:51:03.712 --> 01:51:05.062
But...

1232
01:51:06.525 --> 01:51:09.988
...unfortunately. you killed my mother.

1233
01:51:19.284 --> 01:51:20.704
This is what we're going to do.

1234
01:51:21.064 --> 01:51:23.024
No. please Erik. no.

1235
01:51:23.368 --> 01:51:26.988
I'm going to count to three.
And I'm going to move the coin.

1236
01:51:29.041 --> 01:51:30.254
One...

1237
01:51:32.020 --> 01:51:33.625
Please. Erik.

1238
01:51:41.767 --> 01:51:42.965
Two...

1239
01:51:49.879 --> 01:51:50.992
Three.

1240
01:51:52.846 --> 01:51:54.790
Aaaaaaaah!

1241
01:52:20.219 --> 01:52:23.057
The Russians share our concerns.

1242
01:52:23.310 --> 01:52:25.989
And will join a strike on all the mutants.

1243
01:52:26.271 --> 01:52:28.312
We can end this threat for good.

1244
01:52:28.540 --> 01:52:30.418
We'll never have another opportunity like this.

1245
01:52:30.485 --> 01:52:32.129
We have an agent on that beach.

1246
01:52:32.429 --> 01:52:35.555
- One agent.
- She's a good agent.

1247
01:52:35.811 --> 01:52:37.257
She's collateral damage.

1248
01:52:43.176 --> 01:52:45.332
Today our fighting stops.

1249
01:53:10.016 --> 01:53:12.874
Take off your blinders. brothers and sisters.

1250
01:53:13.244 --> 01:53:14.974
The real enemy is out there.

1251
01:53:16.771 --> 01:53:18.977
I feel their guns moving in the water.

1252
01:53:19.292 --> 01:53:21.485
Their metal targeting us.

1253
01:53:21.815 --> 01:53:25.629
Americans. Soviets. humans.

1254
01:53:26.797 --> 01:53:28.881
United in their fear of the unknown.

1255
01:53:30.313 --> 01:53:33.573
A Neanderthal is running scared.
my fellow mutants.

1256
01:53:36.374 --> 01:53:37.647
Go ahead. Charles.

1257
01:53:39.922 --> 01:53:41.403
Tell me I'm wrong.

1258
01:54:01.657 --> 01:54:04.448
Fleet commander this is X-ray Bravo-7-zero.

1259
01:54:04.670 --> 01:54:05.913
Respond. over.

1260
01:54:07.145 --> 01:54:09.723
The beach is secure. call off the attack.

1261
01:54:09.809 --> 01:54:12.238
The beach is targeted and ready to
be fired upon. sir.

1262
01:54:12.429 --> 01:54:14.342
- Stand by.
- Officer: Standing by. sir.

1263
01:54:18.767 --> 01:54:19.810
Hello?

1264
01:54:21.950 --> 01:54:22.992
Hello!

1265
01:54:31.081 --> 01:54:33.759
- Fire.
- Fire.

1266
01:55:22.136 --> 01:55:24.129
Erik. you said yourself. we're the better men.

1267
01:55:24.992 --> 01:55:26.371
This is the time to prove it.

1268
01:55:30.435 --> 01:55:32.509
There are thousands of men on those ships.

1269
01:55:32.510 --> 01:55:34.311
getting orders. innocent men.

1270
01:55:34.898 --> 01:55:36.653
They're just following orders.

1271
01:55:38.838 --> 01:55:41.295
I've been at the mercy of men
just following orders.

1272
01:55:45.848 --> 01:55:47.215
Never again.

1273
01:55:51.843 --> 01:55:53.205
Erik. release them.

1274
01:56:00.121 --> 01:56:01.700
Noooo!

1275
01:56:07.633 --> 01:56:09.865
I don't want to hurt you.
don't make me.

1276
01:56:10.960 --> 01:56:12.256
Stay back!

1277
01:56:14.971 --> 01:56:16.168
Charles. enough.

1278
01:56:21.140 --> 01:56:22.279
Erik. stop!

1279
01:56:32.713 --> 01:56:35.263
Gentlemen. it's been an honor serving with you.

1280
01:57:26.503 --> 01:57:27.979
I said back off!

1281
01:57:30.157 --> 01:57:32.603
You. you did this!

1282
01:57:36.772 --> 01:57:40.296
Please...

1283
01:57:41.377 --> 01:57:45.156
She didn't do this. Erik.
You did.

1284
01:57:53.105 --> 01:57:56.775
Us turning on each other.
it's what they want.

1285
01:57:57.142 --> 01:57:59.087
I tried to warn you. Charles.

1286
01:58:01.528 --> 01:58:05.692
I want you by my side.
We're brothers. you and I.

1287
01:58:06.459 --> 01:58:09.395
All of us. together. Protecting each other.

1288
01:58:11.558 --> 01:58:13.389
We want the same thing.

1289
01:58:14.773 --> 01:58:16.192
Oh. my friend.

1290
01:58:16.915 --> 01:58:20.173
I'm sorry. but we do not.

1291
01:58:36.445 --> 01:58:42.277
- Charles. I'm sorry. I'm so sorry. Charles.
- Charles: It's all right. it's all right.

1292
01:58:46.398 --> 01:58:48.466
His society won't accept us.

1293
01:58:49.802 --> 01:58:51.412
We form our own.

1294
01:58:51.521 --> 01:58:53.591
The humans have played their hand.

1295
01:58:55.874 --> 01:58:58.219
Now we get ready to play ours.

1296
01:59:01.016 --> 01:59:02.381
Who's with me?

1297
01:59:13.997 --> 01:59:15.454
No more hiding.

1298
01:59:41.814 --> 01:59:46.356
You. you should go with him.
It's what you want.

1299
01:59:47.110 --> 01:59:49.307
You promised me you would never read my mind.

1300
01:59:49.857 --> 01:59:50.812
I know.

1301
01:59:51.421 --> 01:59:54.037
I promised you a great many things.
I'm afraid.

1302
01:59:54.824 --> 01:59:55.850
I'm sorry.

1303
02:00:01.252 --> 02:00:02.648
Take care of him.

1304
02:00:18.109 --> 02:00:20.740
And Beast. never forget.

1305
02:00:21.671 --> 02:00:24.706
Mutant and proud.

1306
02:00:33.196 --> 02:00:34.569
Help me out. help him.

1307
02:00:35.655 --> 02:00:37.167
I'm going to get you to a hospital.

1308
02:00:37.168 --> 02:00:40.512
- Wait. don't. Charles. don't move. okay.

1309
02:00:40.513 --> 02:00:46.054
All right. actually I ca.....I...I...

1310
02:00:48.250 --> 02:00:49.622
I can't feel my legs

1311
02:00:51.724 --> 02:00:53.355
I can't feel my legs.

1312
02:00:55.413 --> 02:00:57.084
I can't feel my legs.

1313
02:01:08.928 --> 02:01:12.545
<i>In this week of thanksgiving.
There is much for which we can be grateful.</i>

1314
02:01:12.752 --> 02:01:16.066
<i>As you look back to where we stood.
only four weeks ago.</i>

1315
02:01:16.358 --> 02:01:19.469
<i>The unity of this hemisphere.
the support of our allies.</i>

1316
02:01:19.640 --> 02:01:22.164
<i>And the calm determination of the American people.</i>

1317
02:01:22.656 --> 02:01:25.338
<i>These qualities may be tested many more times.</i>

1318
02:01:25.573 --> 02:01:26.827
<i>In this decade.</i>

1319
02:01:30.010 --> 02:01:32.384
So how many students
do you think you'll have here?

1320
02:01:32.385 --> 02:01:34.425
Once you get the academy up and running.

1321
02:01:34.929 --> 02:01:38.790
As many as I can manage. Possibly more.

1322
02:01:41.812 --> 02:01:46.401
You know. one day the government is going
to realize how lucky they were.

1323
02:01:46.606 --> 02:01:48.306
...to have Professor X on their side.

1324
02:01:49.932 --> 02:01:52.283
I guess I've been on the
road to a professor now. aren't I.

1325
02:01:52.284 --> 02:01:53.937
Next thing I'll be going bald.

1326
02:01:55.751 --> 02:01:57.946
We're still on the government’s side. Moira.

1327
02:01:58.518 --> 02:02:01.186
Still a G-man. just without the G.

1328
02:02:01.573 --> 02:02:04.418
No. you're your own team now.

1329
02:02:05.232 --> 02:02:06.363
It's better.

1330
02:02:07.440 --> 02:02:10.183
You're. "X-Men".

1331
02:02:12.423 --> 02:02:13.902
Yes. I like the sound of that.

1332
02:02:14.434 --> 02:02:20.398
Moira. for us anonymity will be the first line of defense.

1333
02:02:20.399 --> 02:02:21.721
I know.

1334
02:02:23.365 --> 02:02:27.096
They can threaten me all they want. Charles.

1335
02:02:27.935 --> 02:02:30.194
I'll never tell them where you are.

1336
02:02:30.799 --> 02:02:31.842
Ever.

1337
02:02:32.775 --> 02:02:34.438
I know you won't.

1338
02:02:36.338 --> 02:02:37.393
My love.

1339
02:02:45.024 --> 02:02:47.326
I remember the attack on HQ.

1340
02:02:47.913 --> 02:02:49.668
Leaving to go somewhere else.

1341
02:02:50.323 --> 02:02:53.502
And then this morning. I woke up at home.

1342
02:02:54.346 --> 02:02:55.388
That's it.

1343
02:02:56.612 --> 02:02:58.808
All that time wiped clean from your mind.

1344
02:02:59.172 --> 02:03:00.312
Just gone.

1345
02:03:00.693 --> 02:03:02.723
He can do that.
You don't remember anything?

1346
02:03:03.298 --> 02:03:11.058
Sometimes I get fragments.
Like trees. sunlight.

1347
02:03:13.219 --> 02:03:16.073
- A kiss.
- Aw. Jesus.

1348
02:03:16.614 --> 02:03:20.101
Gentlemen. this is why the CIA
is no place for a woman.

1349
02:03:25.131 --> 02:03:26.250
What the hell was that?

1350
02:03:42.985 --> 02:03:45.209
I know we've had our differences.

1351
02:03:47.849 --> 02:03:51.758
- Where's your telepath friend?
- Erik: Gone.

1352
02:03:52.799 --> 02:03:55.937
Left a bit of a gap in my life.
If I'm to be honest.

1353
02:03:55.938 --> 02:03:57.889
I was rather hoping you would fill it.

1354
02:04:03.274 --> 02:04:04.340
Join us.

1355
02:04:11.791 --> 02:04:13.203
Erik. I believe.

1356
02:04:16.571 --> 02:04:18.291
I prefer...

1357
02:04:20.286 --> 02:04:21.189
...Magneto.

1358
02:04:22.305 --> 02:05:22.287
